// The aliasing half of D-004: `$$m` EXCLUDES, `$$i` SHARES, `@` claims nothing
// (1.5.5 step 1; D-286 as recommended in S-60).
//
// Written where the escape analysis left off. 0.5.1 said of `$$i`/`$$m`: "the
// aliasing rules that make `$$i` many-readers and `$$m` exclusive … a different
// question and not settled here" -- and until this pass the two spellings built
// one node the checker typed as `T->`, the bindings analysis read `$$m` as the
// write that fills a destination (D-118), the escape analysis treated both as
// `@`, and nothing else told them apart: two `$$m` of one element, or a `$$m x`
// held while `x` was assigned and then written through the pointer, compiled
// and ran (measured 2026-09-11: exit 32).
//
// THE VOCABULARY (meta/roadmap/done/1.5/1.5.5.md §2.1). A CLAIM is a `$$i place`
// (shared: many readers) or `$$m place` (exclusive: one writer, no other name).
// `@place` is a PLAIN ADDRESS: it claims nothing and says nothing about
// direction. An ACCESS is any way source reaches storage under a root -- a
// read, a write, an address of either spelling, a `move`, the implicit address
// a pointer-receiver call takes, a range view, a `pick` selector; an access is
// WRITE-CAPABLE unless it is a plain read, because the pointer type carries no
// mutability and whatever holds an address may write through it. A claim's
// ROOT is the identifier at the bottom of its place path (`place_root`); its
// PATH the steps outward, each a field name or an index (a NUMERAL when the
// folder knows it, COMPUTED otherwise). Two paths under one root OVERLAP when
// every field step of their common prefix names the same field and every index
// pair the same element; they are STATICALLY DISJOINT when a field differs or
// two numerals differ, STATICALLY OVERLAPPING when nothing along the prefix is
// computed, COMPUTED otherwise.
//
// THE LIFETIME OF A CLAIM IS LEXICAL (§2.2; non-lexical lifetimes and the
// prototype's two-phase borrows are decided OUT with D-004's "no lifetime
// inference"). A whole call argument or receiver lives for that call and
// conflicts with the call's other arguments and receiver; the whole initialiser
// or assigned value of a pointer local is HELD by that local from its
// DECLARATION to the end of the block that declares it -- the holder's whole
// scope, since a loop reaches every statement after the declaration again
// after an assignment. A holder's own uses (`<-p`, `p.f`, passing `p`) are the
// claim's uses, not accesses of the root. A `defer` body runs at its block's
// exit and is checked against every party of the enclosing blocks at any
// position. A holder is USED, NOT COPIED; a claim standing anywhere else -- a
// literal, a `pass` value, nested in another expression, assigned to a
// non-local place, an argument of a call whose result can carry a pointer
// (D-117 rule A: the callee decides what the result points at) -- is refused
// by name (BORROW-014) with the fix in the sentence: "spell `@` for an address
// that claims nothing". `$$i`/`$$m` STATE intent; this pass follows exactly the
// shapes it can honour and refuses the rest, the D-019 pattern.
//
// THE CONFLICTS (§2.4), checked at every access whose root is a live party's:
//
//     party \ access   | a read      | write-capable
//     shared  (`$$i`)  | fine        | BORROW-013
//     exclusive (`$$m`)| BORROW-013  | BORROW-013
//     plain (`@` held) | fine unless the access is a CLAIM
//
// A conflict over statically disjoint paths is nothing; over statically
// overlapping paths it is BORROW-013 naming the party; over computed paths it
// is a GUARD SITE -- at this step still BORROW-013 (the plan's conservative
// refusal), at step 2 the byte-range compare the verified build elides. A
// write-capable access rooted at a SHARED claim's holder is BORROW-013 too:
// shared means readers. WHAT THIS CHECKS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT: exclusivity is
// decided among accesses that spell the SAME ROOT; two pointer bindings that
// alias one storage are two roots, and a claim through one is not seen from
// the other -- a syntactic path analysis cannot know two names alias, and
// making every pointer parameter exclusive would refuse the compiler's own
// architecture (every walker holds pointers to shared state).
//
// ONE FORWARD WALK, NO FIXPOINT: because a holder is never copied, every party
// is admitted at exactly one site (a declaration's initialiser, an assignment's
// value, a call's argument), and a pre-scan of the function's assignments
// registers an assignment-admitted party at its holder's DECLARATION, which is
// where the holder's scope begins. FAIL CLOSED like every walk here: a
// statement or expression kind without an entry is BORROW-008, the escape
// walk's internal code, and the depth bound refuses rather than guesses.
mod:alias;

use "../source_location.npk".*;
use "../ast_kind.npk".*;
use "../ast.npk".*;
use "../intern.npk".*;
use "../diagnostics.npk".*;
use "../symbols.npk".*;
use "../parse_expr.npk".*;
use "../parse_stmt.npk".*;
use "../parse_pick.npk".*;
use "../parse_decl.npk".*;
use "../parser.npk".*;
use "../types.npk".*;
use "../type_layout.npk".*;     // type_is_list: a `List` element address freezes the `List` (DEF-304)
use "../type_resolve.npk".*;
use "../type_members.npk".*;   // type_param_at_of: the receiver's parameter
use "../expr_types.npk".*;
use "./analysis_codes.npk".*;
use "./escape.npk".*;          // carries_pointer (pub since 1.5.5 step 1)

pub func:ALIAS_DEPTH = int32() never fails { pass (raw AST_DEPTH_MAX()); };  // the one bound (DEF-150's c2, 1.6.1e step 2)

// The three party kinds, and the four access kinds.
pub func:PARTY_PLAIN = int32() never fails     { pass 0i32; };
pub func:PARTY_SHARED = int32() never fails    { pass 1i32; };
pub func:PARTY_EXCLUSIVE = int32() never fails { pass 2i32; };
// A VIEW (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0): a shared party the language makes for the author
// -- readers fine, every write-capable access of the root refused (BORROW-015)
// -- held by the binding that holds the view for its whole scope, or live for
// the call a view expression is an argument of.
pub func:PARTY_VIEW = int32() never fails      { pass 3i32; };
// A LENT CROSSING (DEF-148, 1.6.1e step 1): a spawn's `@s` of one of D-180's
// five kinds, live from the spawn to the end of its block (the join) -- every
// write-capable access of the root refused (BORROW-016) except the receiver of
// an operation in the kind's concurrent set, and `@s` to a callee judged, as a
// view's is, by what the callee's summary writes.
pub func:PARTY_LENT = int32() never fails      { pass 4i32; };
// A PLAIN ADDRESS INTO A `List` ELEMENT (DEF-304, landing 162): `@l[i]`, a view-
// like party (D-325) -- the `List` root is FROZEN against a reallocating or
// dropping operation while the address is live, as a viewed root is frozen
// against a write. Caught exactly where a view is (the mutation-summary path,
// `summary_judged`), reported BORROW-015, differing only in the sentence.
pub func:PARTY_ELEM_ADDR = int32() never fails { pass 5i32; };
pub func:ACC_READ = int32() never fails        { pass 0i32; };
pub func:ACC_WRITE = int32() never fails       { pass 1i32; };
pub func:ACC_SHARED = int32() never fails      { pass 2i32; };
pub func:ACC_EXCLUSIVE = int32() never fails   { pass 3i32; };

// The overlap classes.
pub func:OV_DISJOINT = int32() never fails { pass 0i32; };
pub func:OV_STATIC = int32() never fails   { pass 1i32; };
pub func:OV_COMPUTED = int32() never fails { pass 2i32; };

pub struct:Party = {
    ExprId:site;       // the `$$i`/`$$m`/`@` expression, or the view expression
    int32:kind;        // PARTY_*
    int32:root;        // the root symbol
    int32:holder;      // the holder's symbol, or 0 for a call-duration party
    ExprId:place;      // the claimed or viewed PLACE (the operand of a claim; a view's viewed place)
    int32:view_kind;   // a VIEW party's provenance (VIEW_DIRECT / VIEW_LAUNDERED), 0 otherwise
    bool:root_ptr;     // the root is a POINTER binding: its own reassignment leaves the viewed pointee alone
    int32:path;        // a VIEW party's steps BELOW its place, the escape analysis's interned path (0: none)
};

pub struct:Alias = {
    Ast->:ast;
    SymbolTable->:tab;
    TypeTable->:types;
    ExprTypes->:etypes;
    InternTable->:it;
    DiagList->:diags;
    TypeResolver->:tr;
    Escape->:esc;              // the view references a binding holds (D-325), computed at the escape fixpoint
    int32:scope;               // the module scope the function is folded in
    List<Party>:live;          // the live parties, a stack
    List<int64>:frames;        // the block marks into `live`
    List<Party>:pre;           // every party of the function, by admission site
    List<int64>:call_marks;    // the mark before each open call's parties
    // THE SYMBOL A VAR-DECL STATEMENT DECLARED, by statement index (a name
    // may be shadowed, so the origin decides): built once from the table.
    wild int32->:stmt_sym;
    int32:stmt_count;
    // THE SYMBOL A DECLARATION MADE (a parameter), by declaration index.
    wild int32->:decl_sym;
    int32:decl_count;
    // THE SPAWN BEING WALKED (DEF-148): the call under a `drop` whose callee is
    // `async`, while its arguments are walked; none otherwise.
    ExprId:spawn_call;
    // THE RECEIVER OF A CONCURRENT-SET OPERATION is checked against every party
    // but the lent ones (DEF-148), for that one access.
    bool:skip_lent;
};

pub func:alias_init = Alias(Ast->:ast, SymbolTable->:tab, TypeTable->:types,
                            ExprTypes->:etypes, InternTable->:it, DiagList->:diags,
                            TypeResolver->:tr, Escape->:esc) never fails {
    int32:sc = raw ast_stmt_count(ast);
    if (sc < 1i32) { sc = 1i32; }
    wild int8->:mem = alloc((sc => int64) * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int32->:map = mem =>! wild int32->;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...(sc => int64)) { map[i] = 0i32; }
    int32:dc = raw ast_decl_count(ast);
    if (dc < 1i32) { dc = 1i32; }
    wild int8->:dmem = alloc((dc => int64) * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int32->:dmap = dmem =>! wild int32->;
    for (int64:di in 0i64...(dc => int64)) { dmap[di] = 0i32; }
    int32:n = raw symtab_count(tab);
    for (int32:si in 1i32...n) {
        Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(tab, si);
        if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) {
            if ((s.origin >= 0i32) && (s.origin < sc)) { map[s.origin => int64] = si; }
        }
        if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
            if ((s.origin >= 0i32) && (s.origin < dc)) { dmap[s.origin => int64] = si; }
        }
    }
    pass Alias{ ast: ast, tab: tab, types: types, etypes: etypes, it: it, diags: diags, tr: tr,
                esc: esc,
                scope: 0i32,
                live: raw list_init::<Party>(16i64),
                frames: raw list_init::<int64>(16i64),
                pre: raw list_init::<Party>(16i64),
                call_marks: raw list_init::<int64>(8i64),
                stmt_sym: map, stmt_count: sc, decl_sym: dmap, decl_count: dc,
                spawn_call: raw expr_none(), skip_lent: false };
};

// The symbol a declaration (a parameter) made, or 0.
func:decl_symbol_of = int32(Alias->:x, int32:decl) never fails {
    if (decl < 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if (decl >= x.decl_count) { pass 0i32; }
    pass x.decl_sym[decl => int64];
};

func:alias_err = NIL(Alias->:x, move string:code, move string:msg, Span:sp) never fails {
    drop diaglist_push(x.diags, raw diag_error(move(code), move(msg), sp));
    pass NIL;
};

// --- modules and declarations --------------------------------------------------

pub func:alias_module = NIL(Alias->:x, DeclId:mod_id, int32:scope) never fails {
    x.scope = scope;
    DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mod_id);
    int32:n = raw item_member_count(x.ast, m);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        drop alias_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, m, i), scope);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:alias_decl = NIL(Alias->:x, DeclId:id, int32:scope) never fails {
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) {
        StmtId:body = raw fn_body(x.ast, d);
        if (!(raw stmt_is_none(body))) { drop alias_fn(x, d, body); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) {
        int32:inner = raw nested_module_scope(x.tab, d, scope);
        if (inner == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
        int32:saved = x.scope;
        drop alias_module(x, id, inner);
        x.scope = saved;
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclImplDecl) {
        for (int32:j in 0i32...(raw impl_member_count(x.ast, d))) {
            drop alias_decl(x, raw impl_member(x.ast, d, j), scope);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl) {
        for (int32:k in 0i32...(raw item_member_count(x.ast, d))) {
            drop alias_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, d, k), scope);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// ONE FUNCTION: the pre-scan, then the walk over the body with the parameters'
// assignment-admitted parties live from the entry.
func:alias_fn = NIL(Alias->:x, DeclNode:d, StmtId:body) never fails {
    drop list_clear(@x.live);
    drop list_clear(@x.frames);
    drop list_clear(@x.pre);
    drop list_clear(@x.call_marks);
    drop prescan_stmt(x, body, raw ALIAS_DEPTH());
    // A PARAMETER'S POINTEE MAY HOLD VIEWS (D-325): a struct field viewing
    // another field, wired through this pointer here or by a caller -- the
    // parties are the parameter's, live for the whole body.
    int32:npar = raw fn_param_count(x.ast, d);
    for (int32:pi in 0i32...npar) {
        DeclId:pdid = raw fn_param(x.ast, d, pi);
        int32:psym = raw decl_symbol_of(x, pdid.index);
        if (psym == 0i32) { continue; }
        int32:e = raw escape_param_view_ref_first(x.esc, pdid.index);
        while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
            ViewRef:vr = raw escape_view_ref(x.esc, e);
            e = raw escape_view_ref_next(x.esc, e);
            if (vr.root == 0i32) { continue; }
            if ((vr.kind != (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) && (vr.kind != (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) { continue; }
            ExprId:place = ExprId{ index: vr.place };
            drop list_push(@x.pre, Party{ site: place, kind: raw PARTY_VIEW(), root: vr.root, holder: psym,
                                          place: place, view_kind: vr.kind, root_ptr: raw root_ident_is_pointer(x, place),
                                          path: vr.path });
        }
    }
    // A parameter holder's scope is the function: its parties are live at entry.
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.pre.count) {
        Party:pp = x.pre[i];
        if (pp.holder == 0i32) { continue; }
        Symbol:hs = raw symtab_get(x.tab, pp.holder);
        if (hs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) { drop list_push(@x.live, pp); }
    }
    drop alias_stmt(x, body, raw ALIAS_DEPTH());
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the pre-scan: where each held party is admitted ----------------------------
//
// Every var-decl initialiser and every assignment value that IS a claim or a
// plain address into a local holder is recorded with its holder's symbol, so
// the walk can make it live at the holder's DECLARATION (an assignment inside
// a loop reaches every statement after the declaration again) and a `defer`
// body can see the parties of its enclosing blocks at any position.
func:prescan_stmt = NIL(Alias->:x, StmtId:id, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, id);
    int32:dd = depth - 1i32;
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        ExprId:init = raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, s);
        int32:hsym = raw decl_symbol(x, id, raw stmt_name(s));
        int32:pk = raw party_kind_of(x, init);
        if (pk >= 0i32) {
            drop prescan_party(x, init, pk, hsym);
        }
        drop prescan_view_parties(x, id, hsym);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        ExprId:val = raw stmt_assigned(s);
        int32:pk2 = raw party_kind_of(x, val);
        if (pk2 >= 0i32) {
            int32:tsym = raw bare_local_symbol(x, raw stmt_target(s));
            if (tsym != 0i32) { drop prescan_party(x, val, pk2, tsym); }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop prescan_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) }, dd);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_then(s), dd);
        drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_else(s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), dd); pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_body(x.ast, s), dd);
        drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_then(x.ast, s), dd);
        drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_end(x.ast, s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) { drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_for_body(x.ast, s), dd); pass NIL; }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        drop prescan_stmt(x, raw stmt_counted_body(s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:pa in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            drop prescan_stmt(x, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), pa), dd);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickArm) { drop prescan_stmt(x, raw arm_body(s), dd); pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) { drop prescan_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: s.a }, dd); pass NIL; }
    pass NIL;
};

// A PLACE THAT CROSSES A `List` INDEX (DEF-304, landing 162): the operand of an
// `@` whose path indexes a `List` -- `@l[i]`, `@l[i].f`, `@s.items[i]`, `@a[i][j]`
// over a `List` at either level -- is a plain address INTO a `List` element, and
// the buffer it points at is freed when the `List` reallocates (a push that
// grows, a reserve, a truncate, a clear, a pop) or is reassigned, moved out or
// dropped. An index of a FIXED ARRAY is not one (arrays never reallocate: the
// control u304h), nor an index of a SLICE (a view, D-325's own domain).
func:place_is_list_element = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass false; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            ExprId:base = raw expr_lhs(n);
            int32:bt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, base);
            if ((bt != 0i32) && (raw type_is_list(x.tr, bt))) { pass true; }
            cur = base;
            continue;
        }
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// The party kind an admitted value would make, or -1 for an ordinary value:
// `$$i` shared, `$$m` exclusive, `@` plain -- the WHOLE value, nothing nested.
func:party_kind_of = int32(Alias->:x, ExprId:val) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(val)) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, val);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        if (raw borrow_is_mut(n)) { pass (raw PARTY_EXCLUSIVE()); }
        pass (raw PARTY_SHARED());
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        // A plain address INTO a `List` element freezes the `List` (DEF-304).
        if (raw place_is_list_element(x, raw expr_operand(n))) { pass (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()); }
        pass (raw PARTY_PLAIN());
    }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

func:prescan_party = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:site, int32:kind, int32:holder) never fails {
    if (holder == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, site);
    int32:root = raw place_root_symbol(x, raw expr_operand(n));
    if (root == 0i32) { pass NIL; }   // no named root: BORROW-014 at the walk
    drop list_push(@x.pre, Party{ site: site, kind: kind, root: root, holder: holder,
                                  place: raw expr_operand(n), view_kind: 0i32, root_ptr: false, path: 0i32 });
    pass NIL;
};

// THE VIEW PARTIES A DECLARED BINDING HOLDS (D-325): one per view reference the
// escape fixpoint recorded on the declaring statement -- from its initialiser
// and from every assignment into it, so the party is live from the DECLARATION
// as a claim assigned later is. A POINTER binding holds addresses, D-286's plain
// party, and freezes nothing.
func:prescan_view_parties = NIL(Alias->:x, StmtId:sid, int32:holder) never fails {
    if (holder == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw escape_holder_is_pointer(x.esc, sid.index)) { pass NIL; }
    int32:i = raw escape_view_ref_first(x.esc, sid.index);
    while (i >= 0i32) decreases i + 1i32 {
        ViewRef:vr = raw escape_view_ref(x.esc, i);
        i = raw escape_view_ref_next(x.esc, i);
        if (vr.root == 0i32) { continue; }
        // ONLY A VIEW IS A PARTY: a carried parameter value or an address the
        // result kept (D-286's plain party) freezes nothing.
        if ((vr.kind != (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) && (vr.kind != (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) { continue; }
        ExprId:place = ExprId{ index: vr.place };
        drop list_push(@x.pre, Party{ site: place, kind: raw PARTY_VIEW(), root: vr.root, holder: holder,
                                      place: place, view_kind: vr.kind, root_ptr: raw root_ident_is_pointer(x, place),
                                      path: vr.path });
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Is the identifier at a place's root (through views) a pointer binding?
func:root_ident_is_pointer = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, cur, raw BORROW_FUEL());
        if (r.exhausted) { pass false; }
        if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass false; }
        ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
        // AN EXPLICIT `<-` IS A STEP TO THE POINTER'S NAME (DEF-272, landing 138):
        // `(<-p).f` and `p.f` are one storage (D-098), and `(<-lp)[i]` is the one
        // spelling of an element behind a pointer (TYPE-082); a write through
        // either is a write-capable access of what `p` reaches, as the
        // auto-dereference's always was.
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(rn); continue; }
        if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass false; }
        if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
        if (!(raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, rn.a))) {
            int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, r.id);
            if (t == 0i32) { pass false; }
            pass ((raw type_kind(x.types, t)) == (raw TY_POINTER()));
        }
        cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a)).link };
    }
    pass false;
};

// The symbol a var-decl statement declared, from the map built at init.
func:decl_symbol = int32(Alias->:x, StmtId:sid, int32:name) never fails {
    if (sid.index < 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if (sid.index >= x.stmt_count) { pass 0i32; }
    pass x.stmt_sym[sid.index => int64];
};

// A bare local or parameter name as an assignment target, else 0.
func:bare_local_symbol = int32(Alias->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass 0i32; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass 0i32; }
    if (n.a == 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(x.tab, n.a);
    if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass n.a; }
    if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
        DeclNode:dn = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: s.origin });
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) { pass n.a; }
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

// The root symbol of a place, through views (a lending `pick`'s binding stands
// in for its selector's root, D-266), or 0 when the place has no named root.
func:place_root_symbol = int32(Alias->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, cur, raw BORROW_FUEL());
        if (r.exhausted) { pass 0i32; }
        if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(rn); continue; }   // DEF-272: see `root_ident_is_pointer`
        if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass 0i32; }
        if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
        if (!(raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, rn.a))) { pass rn.a; }
        cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a)).link };
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

// --- paths ------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// A step outward from the root: a field (its interned name), an index (its
// expression, and its value when the folder knows it), or a range view (the
// whole extent at that position -- it overlaps every index there). Since
// landing 159 two more kinds are read and compared as a range, and never
// merge with the step after them (`level_steps`): a `pick` binding's opaque
// step, and an element somewhere in an extent (the escape analysis's levelled
// `e<lo>:<hi>` and `E`).
pub struct:Step = {
    int32:kind;      // 0 field, 1 index, 2 range, 3 opaque, 4 an element in an extent
    int32:name;
    ExprId:index;
    bool:numeral;    // an index the folder knows; a range whose BOTH bounds it knows
    int64:value;     // the index; a range's first element
    int64:hi;        // a range's one-past-the-last element (exclusive, whichever spelling)
};

// The steps of a place, root-outward, through views. False when the walk
// exhausted or the place has no named root.
func:path_steps = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, List<Step>->:out) never fails {
    List<Step>:rev = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass false; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
            drop list_push(@rev, Step{ kind: 0i32, name: (raw expr_name(n)) =>! int32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
            cur = raw expr_operand(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            ExprId:ix = raw expr_rhs(n);
            ExprNode:ixn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ix);
            if (ixn.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) {
                // A RANGE WITH BOTH BOUNDS KNOWN is an interval the overlap
                // question can decide (1.6.1 step 0, for the view parties):
                // `..` includes its last element, `...` excludes it
                // (LEXICAL_REFERENCE §5.1; the node's payload says which).
                ConstVal:lo = raw fold_const(x.tr, raw expr_lhs(ixn), x.scope);
                ConstVal:hi = raw fold_const(x.tr, raw expr_rhs(ixn), x.scope);
                bool:rnum = ((lo.kind == (raw CV_INT())) && (hi.kind == (raw CV_INT())));
                int64:hiv = hi.num;
                if (rnum) { if (ixn.payload != 0i64) { hiv = hi.num + 1i64; } }
                drop list_push(@rev, Step{ kind: 2i32, name: 0i32, index: ix, numeral: rnum, value: lo.num, hi: hiv });
            } else {
                ConstVal:cv = raw fold_const(x.tr, ix, x.scope);
                bool:num = (cv.kind == (raw CV_INT()));
                drop list_push(@rev, Step{ kind: 1i32, name: 0i32, index: ix, numeral: num, value: cv.num, hi: 0i64 });
            }
            cur = raw expr_lhs(n);
            continue;
        }
        // AN EXPLICIT `<-` IS NO STEP (DEF-272): `(<-p).f`'s steps are `p.f`'s,
        // and the whole pointee `<-p` is the root with no step -- which is why
        // `check_access_reported`'s pointer-root exemption asks for the bare name.
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            if (n.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
            // THROUGH A VIEW (D-266): the binding stands in for the payload it
            // views; the selector's own path is not spelled, so the view's
            // steps extend the selector's ROOT with an opaque step -- a view is
            // a part of the selector nobody can name here, so it overlaps every
            // part of it (conservative).
            if (raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, n.a)) {
                drop list_push(@rev, Step{ kind: 3i32, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
                cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, n.a)).link };
                continue;
            }
            // root reached: reverse
            int64:k = rev.count;
            while (k > 0i64) decreases k {
                k = k - 1i64;
                drop list_push(out, rev[k]);
            }
            pass true;
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// A RANGE'S ELEMENT IS ITS STORAGE'S ELEMENT (DEF-303, landing 159): `arr[lo...hi][i]`
// is `arr[lo + i]`, so two paths are compared LEVELLED, by the escape analysis's
// rule for its texts (`level_path_text`): a range step and the index, element
// or range step after it stand at ONE position -- the index `lo + i`, the range
// `[lo + c...lo + d]` (which still takes the step after it), when every bound
// added is known and in [0, 2^31); otherwise the element somewhere in the
// range's extent, and a range of a range nobody can add the computed range.
// Unlevelled, every step after a range stood one position too far: `arr[0...2][0].o`
// written against a view of `arr[0].o.x` met `o` against `x` and read the pair
// disjoint. A `pick` binding's opaque step (kind 3) and an element in an extent
// (kind 4) take nothing after them, and leave as the range step they compare
// as; the levelled list holds fields, indexes and ranges alone.
func:level_steps = List<Step>(List<Step>:a) never fails {
    List<Step>:out = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
    bool:open = false;   // the last step pushed is a range that takes the next
    for (int64:i in 0i64...a.count) {
        Step:s = a[i];
        if (open && (out.count > 0i64) && ((s.kind == 1i32) || (s.kind == 2i32) || (s.kind == 4i32))) {
            int64:last = out.count - 1i64;
            Step:pr = out[last];
            bool:known = (pr.numeral && s.numeral && (pr.value >= 0i64) && (pr.value < 2147483648i64)
                          && (s.value >= 0i64) && (s.value < 2147483648i64) && (s.hi >= 0i64) && (s.hi < 2147483648i64));
            if (s.kind == 1i32) {
                if (known) {
                    out[last] = Step{ kind: 1i32, name: 0i32, index: s.index, numeral: true, value: pr.value + s.value, hi: 0i64 };
                }
                // else the range's own extent stands for the element
                open = false;
                continue;
            }
            if (s.kind == 4i32) {
                if (known) {
                    out[last] = Step{ kind: 2i32, name: 0i32, index: s.index, numeral: true, value: pr.value + s.value, hi: pr.value + s.hi };
                }
                open = false;
                continue;
            }
            // a range of the range: still a range, taking the step after it
            if (known) {
                out[last] = Step{ kind: 2i32, name: 0i32, index: s.index, numeral: true, value: pr.value + s.value, hi: pr.value + s.hi };
            } else {
                out[last] = Step{ kind: 2i32, name: 0i32, index: s.index, numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 };
            }
            continue;
        }
        if ((s.kind == 3i32) || (s.kind == 4i32)) {
            drop list_push(@out, Step{ kind: 2i32, name: 0i32, index: s.index, numeral: s.numeral, value: s.value, hi: s.hi });
            open = false;
            continue;
        }
        drop list_push(@out, s);
        open = (s.kind == 2i32);
    }
    pass out;
};

// The overlap class of two paths under one root, and whether a computed pair
// exists along the common prefix -- the two compared LEVELLED (`level_steps`,
// DEF-303, landing 159).
func:overlap_class = int32(Alias->:x, List<Step>:a0, List<Step>:b0) never fails {
    List<Step>:a = raw level_steps(a0);
    List<Step>:b = raw level_steps(b0);
    int64:n = a.count;
    if (b.count < n) { n = b.count; }
    bool:computed = false;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...n) {
        Step:sa = a[i];
        Step:sb = b[i];
        if ((sa.kind == 0i32) && (sb.kind == 0i32)) {
            if (sa.name != sb.name) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
            continue;
        }
        if ((sa.kind == 1i32) && (sb.kind == 1i32)) {
            if (sa.numeral && sb.numeral) {
                if (sa.value != sb.value) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
                continue;
            }
            computed = true;
            continue;
        }
        // TWO RANGES, OR A RANGE AND AN INDEX, BOTH KNOWN: intervals decide
        // (1.6.1 step 0). `l[0...2]` against `l[3]` or `l[2...4]` is disjoint;
        // a bound the folder does not know keeps the conservative answer
        // below -- the extent overlaps -- never a guard site, since a view's
        // extent has no run-time compare.
        if ((sa.kind == 2i32) && (sb.kind == 2i32)) {
            if (sa.numeral && sb.numeral) {
                if ((sa.hi <= sb.value) || (sb.hi <= sa.value)) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
            }
            continue;
        }
        if ((sa.kind == 2i32) && (sb.kind == 1i32)) {
            if (sa.numeral && sb.numeral) {
                if ((sb.value < sa.value) || (sb.value >= sa.hi)) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
            }
            continue;
        }
        if ((sa.kind == 1i32) && (sb.kind == 2i32)) {
            if (sa.numeral && sb.numeral) {
                if ((sa.value < sb.value) || (sa.value >= sb.hi)) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
            }
            continue;
        }
        // A FIELD AGAINST AN INDEX OR A RANGE at one position: only the prelude's
        // `List` admits both, and its `count` and `cap` are its header, not an
        // element -- disjoint from every element access. Its `items` is the
        // buffer the elements live in: a write to it (a reallocation) frees a
        // slice's storage (`l[lo...hi]`) and overlaps it, and moves an
        // element's HEADER without touching the heap body behind its `ptr` --
        // a view of that body (`l[i].ptr` and below) is disjoint from it
        // (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0: interning more strings does not free the
        // earlier ones a view names). Any other field against an element:
        // the extent overlaps, the closed direction.
        if ((sa.kind == 0i32) && (sb.kind != 0i32)) {
            if (raw header_field_disjoint(x, sa.name, b, i + 1i64, sb.kind)) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
            continue;
        }
        if ((sb.kind == 0i32) && (sa.kind != 0i32)) {
            if (raw header_field_disjoint(x, sb.name, a, i + 1i64, sa.kind)) { pass (raw OV_DISJOINT()); }
            continue;
        }
        continue;
    }
    if (computed) { pass (raw OV_COMPUTED()); }
    pass (raw OV_STATIC());
};

// A PATH DECODED (D-325): the escape analysis's interned text of steps below a
// place -- `f<name>`, `i<n>`, `x`, `r<lo>:<hi>`, `R`, and since landing 159 `P`,
// `e<lo>:<hi>`, `E`, `/`-separated -- appended as `Step`s to a list. A token
// this reader does not know is an opaque step (overlaps everything at its
// position: the closed direction).
func:decode_path = NIL(Alias->:x, int32:path, List<Step>->:out) never fails {
    if (path == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    string:t = raw intern_get(x.it, path);
    fixed uint8[]:b = string_bytes(t);   // the bridge's view is read-only (D-351)
    int64:i = 0i64;
    while (i < b.len) decreases b.len - i {
        int64:j = i;
        while (j < b.len) decreases b.len - j {
            if (b[j] == 47u8) { break; }   // '/'
            j = j + 1i64;
        }
        drop decode_step(x, b, i, j, out);
        i = j + 1i64;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:decode_step = NIL(Alias->:x, fixed uint8[]:b, int64:lo, int64:hi, List<Step>->:out) never fails {
    if (lo >= hi) { pass NIL; }
    uint8:c = b[lo];
    if (c == 102u8) {   // 'f'
        drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: 0i32, name: (raw decode_int(b, lo + 1i64, hi)) =>! int32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (c == 105u8) {   // 'i'
        drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: 1i32, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: true, value: raw decode_int(b, lo + 1i64, hi), hi: 0i64 });
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (c == 120u8) {   // 'x'
        drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: 1i32, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((c == 114u8) || (c == 101u8)) {   // 'r' lo:hi, a range; 'e' lo:hi, an element in that extent
        int32:ek = 2i32;
        if (c == 101u8) { ek = 4i32; }
        int64:colon = lo + 1i64;
        while (colon < hi) decreases hi - colon {
            if (b[colon] == 58u8) { break; }
            colon = colon + 1i64;
        }
        if (colon >= hi) {
            drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: ek, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
            pass NIL;
        }
        drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: ek, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: true,
                                  value: raw decode_int(b, lo + 1i64, colon), hi: raw decode_int(b, colon + 1i64, hi) });
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (c == 82u8) {   // 'R', a computed range
        drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: 2i32, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (c == 69u8) {   // 'E', an element in an extent nobody knows
        drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: 4i32, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
        pass NIL;
    }
    // 'P', a `pick` binding's opaque step, and any token this reader does not know
    drop list_push(out, Step{ kind: 3i32, name: 0i32, index: raw expr_none(), numeral: false, value: 0i64, hi: 0i64 });
    pass NIL;
};

// A decimal integer (a leading '-' allowed) between two byte offsets.
func:decode_int = int64(fixed uint8[]:b, int64:lo, int64:hi) never fails {
    int64:v = 0i64;
    bool:neg = false;
    int64:i = lo;
    if (i < hi) { if (b[i] == 45u8) { neg = true; i = i + 1i64; } }
    while (i < hi) decreases hi - i {
        uint8:c = b[i];
        if ((c < 48u8) || (c > 57u8)) { break; }
        v = (v * 10i64) + ((c - 48u8) => int64);
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    if (neg) { pass (0i64 - v); }
    pass v;
};

// A PARTY'S STEPS: its place's, then its path's (D-325).
func:party_steps = bool(Alias->:x, Party:p, List<Step>->:out) never fails {
    if (!(raw path_steps(x, p.place, out))) { pass false; }
    drop decode_path(x, p.path, out);
    pass true;
};

// Is this field, met against an element step of the other path, one of the
// `List` header fields the element access leaves alone? `other` is the other
// path, `next` the position after its element step, `ekind` that step's kind.
func:header_field_disjoint = bool(Alias->:x, int32:name, List<Step>:other, int64:next, int32:ekind) never fails {
    string:fname = raw intern_get(x.it, name);
    if (raw string_eq(fname, "count")) { pass true; }
    if (raw string_eq(fname, "cap"))   { pass true; }
    if (raw string_eq(fname, "items")) {
        // a slice of the elements' storage dies with the buffer; an element's
        // own heap body (through its `ptr`) does not
        if (ekind == 2i32) { pass false; }
        if (next >= other.count) { pass false; }
        Step:after = other[next];
        if (after.kind != 0i32) { pass false; }
        pass (raw string_eq(raw intern_get(x.it, after.name), "ptr"));
    }
    pass false;
};

// The spelling of a place for a diagnostic: `arr[3]`, `a.b[…]`.
func:render_place = string(Alias->:x, int32:root, List<Step>:steps) never fails {
    string:s = string_concat(raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, root)).name), "");
    for (int64:i in 0i64...steps.count) {
        Step:st = steps[i];
        if (st.kind == 0i32) {
            s = string_concat(s, ".");
            s = string_concat(s, raw intern_get(x.it, st.name));
        }
        if (st.kind == 1i32) {
            if (st.numeral) {
                s = string_concat(s, "[");
                s = string_concat(s, int_to_string(st.value));
                s = string_concat(s, "]");
            } else {
                s = string_concat(s, "[…]");
            }
        }
        if (st.kind == 2i32) {
            if (st.numeral) {
                s = string_concat(s, "[");
                s = string_concat(s, int_to_string(st.value));
                s = string_concat(s, "...");
                s = string_concat(s, int_to_string(st.hi));
                s = string_concat(s, "]");
            } else {
                s = string_concat(s, "[…]");
            }
        }
        if ((st.kind == 3i32) || (st.kind == 4i32)) { s = string_concat(s, "[…]"); }
    }
    pass s;
};

func:party_spelling = string(Alias->:x, Party:p) never fails {
    string:pre = "@";
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) { pre = "$$i "; }
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_EXCLUSIVE())) { pre = "$$m "; }
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) { pre = ""; }
    List<Step>:ps = raw list_init::<Step>(4i64);
    if (!(raw party_steps(x, p, @ps))) { pass (string_concat(pre, "…")); }
    pass (string_concat(pre, raw render_place(x, p.root, ps)));
};

func:party_word = string(Alias->:x, Party:p) never fails {
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) { pass "the shared claim"; }
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_EXCLUSIVE())) { pass "the exclusive claim"; }
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) {
        if (p.view_kind == (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED())) { pass "the possible view (through a call that was handed the place, D-004 rule A) of"; }
        pass "the view of";
    }
    if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR())) { pass "the plain address into a `List` element"; }
    pass "the plain address held by a binding";
};

// --- the conflict check at one access ---------------------------------------------

// Does an access of this kind conflict with a party of that kind?
func:conflicts = bool(int32:pkind, int32:akind) never fails {
    if (pkind == (raw PARTY_EXCLUSIVE())) { pass true; }
    if ((pkind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) || (pkind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) || (pkind == (raw PARTY_LENT()))
        || (pkind == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()))) {
        // a plain address into a `List` element is view-like (DEF-304): a write-
        // capable access of the `List` reallocates and frees the element.
        pass ((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE())));
    }
    // a plain address: only a claim conflicts
    pass ((akind == (raw ACC_SHARED())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE())));
};

func:access_word = string(int32:akind) never fails {
    if (akind == (raw ACC_READ())) { pass "this read"; }
    if (akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) { pass "this write-capable access"; }
    if (akind == (raw ACC_SHARED())) { pass "this shared claim (`$$i`)"; }
    pass "this exclusive claim (`$$m`)";
};

// AN ACCESS OF A PLACE: classified against every live party of the same root.
// `self_site` excludes the access's own party (a claim argument is live for
// its call and is not its own conflict).
pub func:CHECK_ALL = int32() never fails    { pass 0i32; };
pub func:CHECK_CLAIMS = int32() never fails { pass 1i32; };   // the claims and plain addresses, never a view party
pub func:CHECK_VIEWS = int32() never fails  { pass 2i32; };   // the view AND lent parties: those a callee's summary judges (D-325, DEF-148)
pub func:CHECK_LENT = int32() never fails   { pass 3i32; };   // the lent parties alone (a spawn's own arguments, DEF-148)

func:check_access = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:akind, ExprId:self_site, Span:at) never fails {
    drop check_access_ex(x, place, 0i32, akind, self_site, at, raw CHECK_ALL());
    pass NIL;
};

// AN ACCESS OF A PLACE, `extra` a path BELOW it (D-325: what a callee writes
// through what it was handed), `mode` which parties are asked.
func:check_access_ex = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:extra, int32:akind, ExprId:self_site, Span:at,
                           int32:mode) never fails {
    discard(raw check_access_reported(x, place, extra, akind, self_site, at, mode));
    pass NIL;
};

// The same, answering whether a conflict was reported (one mistake, one
// report: a callee's several written paths stop at the first conflict).
func:check_access_reported = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:extra, int32:akind, ExprId:self_site, Span:at,
                                  int32:mode) never fails {
    int32:root = raw place_root_symbol(x, place);
    if (root == 0i32) {
        // A WRITE THROUGH A CALL-RESULT POINTER (DEF-305, landing 161): a pointer
        // that is a call's result -- `wp(raw idp(@h))`, `(raw idp(@h)).set()` --
        // has no named root, so the same-root loop below never runs and the
        // DEF-302 readers at the function's tail are never reached. Resolve it
        // here by rule A to the storage it points at and check the views there
        // (`check_pointer_targets`' call-result arm, which `ptr_write_base`
        // sends every rootless pointer place to). Before the shared-holder case,
        // under the same guard as the named-pointer reader (`mode != CHECK_CLAIMS`,
        // the claims keep D-286's same-root rule).
        if (((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE()))) && (mode != (raw CHECK_CLAIMS()))) {
            int32:plt0 = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, place);
            if ((plt0 != 0i32) && ((raw type_kind(x.types, plt0)) == (raw TY_POINTER()))) {
                List<Step>:ap0 = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
                drop decode_path(x, extra, @ap0);
                if (raw check_pointer_targets(x, place, ap0, akind, at, mode)) { pass true; }
            }
        }
        // NO NAMED ROOT: a place that bottoms in a DEREFERENCE of a shared
        // holder (`@(<-r)` handed to a writer, DEF-123 (a)) is the holder's
        // storage written through it; every other rootless place is nobody's.
        if (((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE()))) && (mode != (raw CHECK_VIEWS()))) {
            pass (raw refuse_shared_holder_write(x, raw deref_holder_of(x, place), at));
        }
        pass false;
    }
    List<Step>:ap = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
    if (!(raw path_steps(x, place, @ap))) { pass false; }
    drop decode_path(x, extra, @ap);
    // A WRITE THROUGH A SHARED CLAIM'S HOLDER: shared means readers.
    if (((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE()))) && (mode != (raw CHECK_VIEWS()))) {
        if (raw refuse_shared_holder_write(x, root, at)) { pass true; }
    }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.live.count) {
        Party:p = x.live[i];
        if (p.root != root) { continue; }
        if (p.site.index == self_site.index) { continue; }
        bool:summary_judged = ((p.kind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) || (p.kind == (raw PARTY_LENT())) || (p.kind == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR())));
        if ((mode == (raw CHECK_VIEWS())) && (!summary_judged)) { continue; }
        if ((mode == (raw CHECK_CLAIMS())) && summary_judged) { continue; }
        if ((mode == (raw CHECK_LENT())) && (p.kind != (raw PARTY_LENT()))) { continue; }
        if (x.skip_lent && (p.kind == (raw PARTY_LENT()))) { continue; }
        // A VIEW PARTY NEVER CONFLICTS WITH THE ACCESS THAT MADE IT: a range
        // view's own creation is the write-capable access of its base (D-249)
        // and the view party's site at once. A LENT party's place IS the
        // spawn's own `@s` operand, and the spawn's callee is read against it
        // on purpose (DEF-148: a task that stores over what it was lent).
        if ((p.kind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) && (p.place.index == place.index) && (extra == 0i32)) { continue; }
        if (!(raw conflicts(p.kind, akind))) { continue; }
        List<Step>:pp = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
        if (!(raw party_steps(x, p, @pp))) { continue; }
        // A POINTER ROOT'S OWN REASSIGNMENT LEAVES THE VIEWED POINTEE ALONE:
        // a view through `Box->:b` is of the pointee's bytes, and `b = other`
        // moves the name, not the storage (the pointee is another owner's;
        // D-286: the pointee is no named root). A write INTO the pointee --
        // `b.s = …`, a path below the root -- is the hazard and stays refused.
        // THE REASSIGNMENT IS THE BARE NAME, WRITTEN DIRECTLY (DEF-272, landing
        // 138): `<-b = …` is zero steps below `b` too and writes the pointee,
        // and a callee's write through `b` (a `CHECK_VIEWS` or `CHECK_LENT`
        // check, the whole pointee an empty path) never reassigns the binding
        // -- neither is exempt.
        if (summary_judged && p.root_ptr && (ap.count == 0i64) && (mode == (raw CHECK_ALL()))
            && ((raw ast_expr(x.ast, place)).kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr)) { continue; }
        int32:cls = raw overlap_class(x, pp, ap);
        if (cls == (raw OV_DISJOINT())) { continue; }
        // A COMPUTED PAIR IS A GUARD SITE (D-286, 1.5.5 step 2): the emitter
        // compares the two storages at run time and traps `BorrowOverlap`,
        // the encoder records the `disjoint` row the verified build elides.
        // A claim's own site is never a guard site of ITSELF; every party the
        // site meets is recorded, and the site keeps its one guard.
        // A VIEW'S EXTENT HAS NO GUARD (D-325): a computed pair against a view
        // party refuses statically, the closed direction.
        if ((cls == (raw OV_COMPUTED())) && (!summary_judged)) {
            drop exprtypes_mark_alias(x.etypes, place.index, p.site.index, p.holder);
            continue;
        }
        // A PLAIN ADDRESS INTO A `List` ELEMENT (DEF-304): view-like, frozen
        // against this reallocating or dropping access; its own distinct
        // sentence, the BORROW-015 code the view shares.
        if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR())) {
            drop report_elem_addr_conflict(x, p, akind, root, ap, cls, at);
            pass true;
        }
        if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) {
            drop report_view_conflict(x, p, akind, root, ap, cls, at);
            pass true;
        }
        if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_LENT())) {
            drop report_lent_conflict(x, p, akind, root, ap, at);
            pass true;
        }
        ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, p.site);
        string:m1 = string_concat(raw access_word(akind), " of `");
        m1 = string_concat(m1, raw render_place(x, root, ap));
        m1 = string_concat(m1, "` conflicts with ");
        m1 = string_concat(m1, raw party_word(x, p));
        m1 = string_concat(m1, " `");
        m1 = string_concat(m1, raw party_spelling(x, p));
        m1 = string_concat(m1, "` at ");
        m1 = string_concat(m1, int_to_string(pn.span.line => int64));
        m1 = string_concat(m1, ":");
        m1 = string_concat(m1, int_to_string(pn.span.col => int64));
        if (p.holder != 0i32) {
            m1 = string_concat(m1, ", live until the end of the block that declares its holder `");
            m1 = string_concat(m1, raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, p.holder)).name));
            m1 = string_concat(m1, "`");
        } else {
            m1 = string_concat(m1, ", live for the call it is an argument of");
        }
        m1 = string_concat(m1, " (D-286): end the claim's scope with a block, or spell `@` for an address that claims nothing");
        drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CONFLICT(), move(m1), at);
        pass true;
    }
    // THROUGH A SLICE NO RANGE NAMES (DEF-297, landing 159): a write through a
    // slice binding or field, or a range of one -- `t[0i64].o = v`, `@t[0i64]` or
    // `t` handed to a writer -- lands in the storage the slice views, whose view
    // parties are rooted THERE: asked at each target (`check_slice_targets`),
    // the claims left to their own rule (D-286).
    if (((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE()))) && (mode != (raw CHECK_CLAIMS()))) {
        ExprId:sb = raw escape_written_slice_base(x.esc, place, (extra != 0i32) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE())));
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(sb))) {
            if (raw check_slice_targets(x, sb, akind, at, mode)) { pass true; }
        }
    }
    // A WRITE THROUGH A POINTER vs A VIEW OF ITS POINTEE BY ANOTHER NAME, and the
    // reverse (DEF-302, landing 160): a view taken through one name and a write
    // through another, one of them a POINTER to the same storage, root at two
    // different symbols and never meet in the same-root loop above. Two readers,
    // the pointer's twin of the slice-targets check: the write through a pointer
    // re-rooted at what the pointer points at, and a write by the pointee's own
    // name against views taken through a pointer at it. The claims keep D-286's
    // same-root rule (`mode != CHECK_CLAIMS`).
    if (((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE()))) && (mode != (raw CHECK_CLAIMS()))) {
        if (raw check_pointer_targets(x, place, ap, akind, at, mode)) { pass true; }
        if (raw check_pointer_view_parties(x, root, ap, akind, at, 0i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A WRITE THROUGH SLICE `sb` AT EACH STORAGE IT VIEWS (DEF-297, DEF-301; landing
// 159): the targets the escape analysis reads off the slice's value
// (`escape_slice_targets`), each checked WHOLE -- the target's own place and
// path, nothing composed below them: a target a value carries transitively is
// a run at another level than the write's -- against the view and lent parties
// rooted at the target's root. A target rooted where the slice itself is
// rooted is the place check's own; every view the slice binding itself holds
// is skipped (`escape_slice_own_holder`, `check_view_parties_at`).
func:check_slice_targets = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:sb, int32:akind, Span:at, int32:mode) never fails {
    int32:own_root = raw place_root_symbol(x, sb);
    int32:own_holder = raw escape_slice_own_holder(x.esc, sb);
    List<ViewRef>:tg = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop escape_slice_targets(x.esc, sb, @tg);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...tg.count) {
        ViewRef:r = tg[i];
        if (r.root == own_root) { continue; }
        List<Step>:ap = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
        if (raw path_steps(x, ExprId{ index: r.place }, @ap)) {
            drop decode_path(x, r.path, @ap);
        } else {
            drop list_truncate(@ap, 0i64);   // the whole root, the closed direction
        }
        if (raw check_view_parties_at(x, r, ap, own_holder, akind, at, mode)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// THE VIEW AND LENT PARTIES ROOTED AT A TARGET's root against a write-capable
// access of the steps `ap` below it -- storage reached through another name (a
// slice's target, DEF-297, landing 159), so no party is the access's own but
// those the slice binding itself holds (`self_holder`, `escape_slice_own_holder`:
// a slice local, or a struct whose one view is its slice field) -- EVERY one of
// them, matched by its holder alone: a slice's parties are its views of the
// runs it spans, and writing an element through it frees none of them. A
// match on the target's place and path as well missed the slice's own view
// whenever the target was spelled otherwise -- `T[]:s = #wild_slice<T>(v.items,
// v.count); s[i] = x;` carries `v`'s own value too (a parameter's value, typed
// as one that may hold the run), whose target is the whole of `v`, so the
// write met `s`'s own view of `v.items` and was refused (the chain's sweep of
// landing 159's first build: five sites of nitpick-time's `Vec` and `Bytes`).
// DEF-275's twin through a pointer is the next reader.
func:check_view_parties_at = bool(Alias->:x, ViewRef:tgt, List<Step>:ap, int32:self_holder, int32:akind,
                                  Span:at, int32:mode) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.live.count) {
        Party:p = x.live[i];
        if (p.root != tgt.root) { continue; }
        if ((p.kind != (raw PARTY_VIEW())) && (p.kind != (raw PARTY_LENT()))) { continue; }
        if ((mode == (raw CHECK_LENT())) && (p.kind != (raw PARTY_LENT()))) { continue; }
        if (x.skip_lent && (p.kind == (raw PARTY_LENT()))) { continue; }
        if ((self_holder != 0i32) && (p.holder == self_holder)) { continue; }
        if (!(raw conflicts(p.kind, akind))) { continue; }
        List<Step>:pp = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
        if (!(raw party_steps(x, p, @pp))) { continue; }
        int32:cls = raw overlap_class(x, pp, ap);
        if (cls == (raw OV_DISJOINT())) { continue; }
        if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_VIEW())) {
            drop report_view_conflict(x, p, akind, tgt.root, ap, cls, at);
            pass true;
        }
        drop report_lent_conflict(x, p, akind, tgt.root, ap, at);
        pass true;
    }
    pass false;
};

// --- a view and a write through a pointer to one storage (DEF-302, landing 160) -----
//
// THE LAST POINTER-TYPED BASE on a place's path (the one nearest the written
// part), or none: `hp.o` answers `hp`, `o.inner.v` answers `o.inner`, `bp.p.o`
// answers `bp.p`.
func:ptr_last_base = ExprId(Alias->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        ExprId:base = raw expr_none();
        bool:found = false;
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) { base = raw expr_operand(n); found = true; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) { base = raw expr_lhs(n); found = true; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { base = raw expr_operand(n); found = true; }
        if (!found) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, base);
        if (t != 0i32) {
            if ((raw type_kind(x.types, t)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass base; }
        }
        cur = base;
    }
    pass (raw expr_none());
};

// THE POINTER an access of `place` with `n` steps goes through: the place itself
// when the access continues past its own steps and it is a pointer (a bare `hp`
// handed a written path below it -- a method's `self.o`), else the last
// pointer-typed base on its path.
func:ptr_write_base = ExprId(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int64:n) never fails {
    List<Step>:own = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
    if (raw path_steps(x, place, @own)) {
        if (n > own.count) {
            int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, place);
            if (t != 0i32) {
                if ((raw type_kind(x.types, t)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass place; }
            }
        }
    }
    pass (raw ptr_last_base(x, place));
};

// IS THIS CHAIN REF A TARGET of a pointer of type `pty` (pointee `pte`)? an
// address whose place IS the pointee type (`hp = @h`), a parameter's value
// carried whose place is the pointer's own type (`hp = p2`).
func:ptr_ref_is_target = bool(Alias->:x, ViewRef:vr, int32:pty, int32:pte) never fails {
    int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, ExprId{ index: vr.place });
    if (pt == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if (vr.kind == (raw REF_ADDR())) { pass (pt == pte); }
    if (vr.kind == (raw REF_PASS())) { pass (pt == pty); }
    pass false;
};

// THE STEPS of a target ref, root-outward (its place's steps, an `@place` peeled,
// plus its interned path below).
func:ptr_target_steps = bool(Alias->:x, ViewRef:vr, List<Step>->:out) never fails {
    ExprId:pl = ExprId{ index: vr.place };
    if (raw expr_is_none(pl)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, pl);
    if (pn.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) { pl = raw expr_operand(pn); }
    if (!(raw path_steps(x, pl, out))) { pass false; }
    drop decode_path(x, vr.path, out);
    pass true;
};

// THE LAST POINTER-TYPED BASE INCLUSIVE of `e` (e itself when it is a pointer,
// else the last pointer base inside it), or none.
func:ptr_base_incl = ExprId(Alias->:x, ExprId:e) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(e)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, e);
    if ((t != 0i32) && ((raw type_kind(x.types, t)) == (raw TY_POINTER()))) { pass e; }
    pass (raw ptr_last_base(x, e));
};

// THE POINTER `pe` IS ITSELF REACHED THROUGH (a two-level pointer): `bp.p` is
// reached through `bp`, `bp.p.q` through `bp.p`; `hp` and `o.inner` (a field of
// a local) through none. The structural base of `pe`'s own outermost step,
// taken to its last pointer base inclusive.
func:ptr_inner_base = ExprId(Alias->:x, ExprId:pe) never fails {
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, pe);
    ExprId:base = raw expr_none();
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) { base = raw expr_operand(n); }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) { base = raw expr_lhs(n); }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { base = raw expr_operand(n); }
    if (raw expr_is_none(base)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    pass (raw ptr_base_incl(x, base));
};

// THE STORAGE A POINTER PLACE `pe` POINTS AT, as target ViewRefs (DEF-302): read
// off the chain of `pe`'s root. A bare pointer local or a pointer field of a
// LOCAL (`hp`, `o.inner`) takes its targets off the root's own chain (`hp = @h`,
// `o.inner = @h` both recorded `@h` there). A pointer reached THROUGH another
// pointer (`bp.p`: `bp = @b`, `b.p = @h`) is resolved one hop at a time -- the
// inner pointer `bp` to its pointees `{b}`, then each pointee's chain for this
// pointer's own targets (`@h` of type `pte`). Fuel-bounded; over-approximate as
// `record_refs_through_indirection` is (any ref of the pointee type is a target).
func:pointer_targets_of = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:pe, int32:fuel, List<ViewRef>->:out) decreases fuel never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(pe)) { pass NIL; }
    int32:r = raw place_root_symbol(x, pe);
    if (r == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, r);
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass NIL; }   // a local's chain holds where it points
    int32:pty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, pe);
    if (pty == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:pte = raw type_elem(x.types, pty);
    ExprId:inner = raw ptr_inner_base(x, pe);
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(inner))) {
        // reached through a pointer: resolve it, then each pointee's chain
        List<ViewRef>:innertgts = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
        drop pointer_targets_of(x, inner, fuel - 1i32, @innertgts);
        for (int64:ii in 0i64...innertgts.count) {
            int32:rr = innertgts[ii].root;
            if (rr == 0i32) { continue; }
            Symbol:rsy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rr);
            if (rsy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { continue; }
            int32:e2 = raw escape_view_ref_first(x.esc, rsy.origin);
            while (e2 >= 0i32) decreases e2 + 1i32 {
                ViewRef:vr2 = raw escape_view_ref(x.esc, e2);
                e2 = raw escape_view_ref_next(x.esc, e2);
                if (vr2.root == 0i32) { continue; }
                if (vr2.root == rr) { continue; }
                if (!(raw ptr_ref_is_target(x, vr2, pty, pte))) { continue; }
                drop list_push(out, vr2);
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    int32:e = raw escape_view_ref_first(x.esc, sy.origin);
    while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
        ViewRef:vr = raw escape_view_ref(x.esc, e);
        e = raw escape_view_ref_next(x.esc, e);
        if (vr.root == 0i32) { continue; }
        if (vr.root == r) { continue; }
        if (!(raw ptr_ref_is_target(x, vr, pty, pte))) { continue; }
        drop list_push(out, vr);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// FORWARD (DEF-302): a write through a pointer -- a pointer local's pointee
// (`hp.o`), a pointer field's, a two-level `bp.p`, a pointer returned or copied --
// re-rooted at each storage the pointer points at (`pointer_targets_of`), the
// write's steps below the pointer composed on, against the view parties THERE
// (`check_view_parties_at`, DEF-297's reader) and the views taken through a
// pointer at the same target (`check_pointer_view_parties`). A bare pointer NAME
// written whole under `CHECK_ALL` is a reassignment (`hp = …`), left alone.
func:check_pointer_targets = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, List<Step>:ap, int32:akind, Span:at, int32:mode) never fails {
    ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, place);
    if ((pn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) && (ap.count == 0i64) && (mode == (raw CHECK_ALL()))) {
        if (raw root_ident_is_pointer(x, place)) { pass false; }
    }
    ExprId:pe = raw ptr_write_base(x, place, ap.count);
    if (raw expr_is_none(pe)) {
        // DEF-305: a pointer that is a CALL'S RESULT (or any pointer expression
        // with NO named root) has no place chain -- resolve it by rule A
        // (`escape_pointer_targets`), the whole write path `ap` composed onto each
        // target. Gated on a ROOTLESS place (`place_root_symbol` 0): a bare NAMED
        // pointer whose `ptr_write_base` is none (a whole-pointee write, `ap`
        // empty) keeps the base's reading -- its reassignment is not a conflict
        // the view/lent readers judge here (D-286, DEF-272), and resolving it
        // would fire on a named pointer's whole-pointee write, outside this
        // defect's scope.
        int32:plt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, place);
        if ((plt != 0i32) && ((raw type_kind(x.types, plt)) == (raw TY_POINTER()))
            && ((raw place_root_symbol(x, place)) == 0i32)) {
            List<ViewRef>:ctg = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
            drop escape_pointer_targets(x.esc, place, @ctg);
            for (int64:ci in 0i64...ctg.count) {
                ViewRef:cvr = ctg[ci];
                List<Step>:ctp = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
                if (!(raw ptr_target_steps(x, cvr, @ctp))) { continue; }
                for (int64:ck in 0i64...ap.count) { drop list_push(@ctp, ap[ck]); }
                if (raw check_view_parties_at(x, cvr, ctp, 0i32, akind, at, mode)) { pass true; }
                if (raw check_pointer_view_parties(x, cvr.root, ctp, akind, at, 0i32)) { pass true; }
            }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    int32:r = raw place_root_symbol(x, pe);
    List<Step>:pre = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
    if (!(raw path_steps(x, pe, @pre))) { pass false; }
    if (pre.count > ap.count) { pass false; }
    List<ViewRef>:tgts = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop pointer_targets_of(x, pe, 8i32, @tgts);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...tgts.count) {
        ViewRef:vr = tgts[i];
        List<Step>:tp = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
        if (!(raw ptr_target_steps(x, vr, @tp))) { continue; }
        for (int64:k in pre.count...ap.count) { drop list_push(@tp, ap[k]); }
        if (raw check_view_parties_at(x, vr, tp, 0i32, akind, at, mode)) { pass true; }
        if (raw check_pointer_view_parties(x, vr.root, tp, akind, at, r)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// REVERSE (DEF-302): a write to `root` at `ap` by the pointee's own name, against
// each live VIEW party taken THROUGH a pointer whose storage includes `root`
// (`vw = string_bytes(hp.o)`, write `h.o`; two-level `bp.p.o`). `skip` is the
// write's own pointer root, when this is called from the forward reader.
func:check_pointer_view_parties = bool(Alias->:x, int32:root, List<Step>:ap, int32:akind, Span:at, int32:skip) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.live.count) {
        Party:p = x.live[i];
        if (p.kind != (raw PARTY_VIEW())) { continue; }
        if (p.root == root) { continue; }
        if ((skip != 0i32) && (p.root == skip)) { continue; }
        if (!(raw conflicts(p.kind, akind))) { continue; }
        List<Step>:pp = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
        if (!(raw party_steps(x, p, @pp))) { continue; }
        ExprId:pe = raw ptr_write_base(x, p.place, pp.count);
        if (raw expr_is_none(pe)) { continue; }
        List<Step>:pre = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
        if (!(raw path_steps(x, pe, @pre))) { continue; }
        if (pre.count > pp.count) { continue; }
        List<ViewRef>:tgts = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
        drop pointer_targets_of(x, pe, 8i32, @tgts);
        for (int64:j in 0i64...tgts.count) {
            ViewRef:vr = tgts[j];
            if (vr.root != root) { continue; }
            List<Step>:tp = raw list_init::<Step>(8i64);
            if (!(raw ptr_target_steps(x, vr, @tp))) { continue; }
            for (int64:k in pre.count...pp.count) { drop list_push(@tp, pp[k]); }
            int32:cls = raw overlap_class(x, tp, ap);
            if (cls == (raw OV_DISJOINT())) { continue; }
            drop report_view_conflict(x, p, akind, root, ap, cls, at);
            pass true;
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A WRITE-CAPABLE ACCESS OF A VIEWED ROOT (D-325, BORROW-015): the message names
// the access, the view, its holder and lifetime, why it is refused, and the fix.
func:report_view_conflict = NIL(Alias->:x, Party:p, int32:akind, int32:root, List<Step>:ap,
                                int32:cls, Span:at) never fails {
    ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, p.site);
    string:m = string_concat(raw access_word(akind), " of `");
    m = string_concat(m, raw render_place(x, root, ap));
    m = string_concat(m, "` conflicts with ");
    m = string_concat(m, raw party_word(x, p));
    m = string_concat(m, " `");
    m = string_concat(m, raw party_spelling(x, p));
    m = string_concat(m, "` at ");
    m = string_concat(m, int_to_string(pn.span.line => int64));
    m = string_concat(m, ":");
    m = string_concat(m, int_to_string(pn.span.col => int64));
    if (p.holder != 0i32) {
        m = string_concat(m, ", held by `");
        m = string_concat(m, raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, p.holder)).name));
        m = string_concat(m, "` until the end of the block that declares it");
    } else {
        m = string_concat(m, ", live for the call it is an argument of");
    }
    if (cls == (raw OV_COMPUTED())) {
        m = string_concat(m, " (a computed index: the view's extent has no run-time guard, so the pair refuses)");
    }
    m = string_concat(m, " -- a view's root is FROZEN while the view is live (D-325): a write that frees or rewrites the viewed bytes would leave the view reading freed memory. End the view's block before writing its root, or make the view a copy (`.clone()`, `string_concat(\"\", …)`)");
    drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_VIEW_ROOT(), move(m), at);
    pass NIL;
};

// A WRITE-CAPABLE ACCESS OF A `List` WHILE A PLAIN ADDRESS INTO ONE OF ITS
// ELEMENTS IS LIVE (DEF-304, D-325, BORROW-015): a push that reallocates, a
// reserve, a truncate, a clear, a pop, a reassignment, a move-out or a drop
// frees the buffer the address points at, as writing a viewed root frees a
// view's bytes. The `List` is FROZEN against the operation while the address is
// live, exactly as D-325 freezes a root against a view; the message differs
// only in the sentence, and the code (BORROW-015) is the view's.
func:report_elem_addr_conflict = NIL(Alias->:x, Party:p, int32:akind, int32:root, List<Step>:ap,
                                     int32:cls, Span:at) never fails {
    ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, p.site);
    string:m = string_concat(raw access_word(akind), " of `");
    m = string_concat(m, raw render_place(x, root, ap));
    m = string_concat(m, "` conflicts with ");
    m = string_concat(m, raw party_word(x, p));
    m = string_concat(m, " `");
    m = string_concat(m, raw party_spelling(x, p));
    m = string_concat(m, "` at ");
    m = string_concat(m, int_to_string(pn.span.line => int64));
    m = string_concat(m, ":");
    m = string_concat(m, int_to_string(pn.span.col => int64));
    if (p.holder != 0i32) {
        m = string_concat(m, ", held by `");
        m = string_concat(m, raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, p.holder)).name));
        m = string_concat(m, "` until the end of the block that declares it");
    } else {
        m = string_concat(m, ", live for the call it is an argument of");
    }
    if (cls == (raw OV_COMPUTED())) {
        m = string_concat(m, " (a computed index: a `List` element address has no run-time guard, so the pair refuses)");
    }
    m = string_concat(m, " -- a `List` is FROZEN while a plain address into one of its elements is live (DEF-304, D-325): a push that reallocates, a reserve, a truncate, a clear, a pop, a reassignment, a move-out or a drop frees the buffer the address points at, leaving it dangling. End the address's block before the operation, or read the element by index (`l[i]`) after it");
    drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_VIEW_ROOT(), move(m), at);
    pass NIL;
};

// A WRITE-CAPABLE ACCESS OF A LENT ROOT (DEF-148, BORROW-016): the message names
// the access, the spawn, the block whose exit joins it, why, and the fix.
func:report_lent_conflict = NIL(Alias->:x, Party:p, int32:akind, int32:root, List<Step>:ap,
                                Span:at) never fails {
    ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, p.site);
    string:m = string_concat(raw access_word(akind), " of `");
    m = string_concat(m, raw render_place(x, root, ap));
    m = string_concat(m, "` conflicts with the task spawned at ");
    m = string_concat(m, int_to_string(pn.span.line => int64));
    m = string_concat(m, ":");
    m = string_concat(m, int_to_string(pn.span.col => int64));
    m = string_concat(m, ", which holds `");
    m = string_concat(m, raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, root)).name));
    m = string_concat(m, "` until the end of this block, whose exit joins it (D-180, D-207): `destroy`, an assignment, a `move` or `$$m` before the join would end a value the task still holds -- destroy it after the block, or join first; the kind's own concurrent operations and `$$i` stay");
    drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_LENT_ROOT(), move(m), at);
    pass NIL;
};

// --- statements ---------------------------------------------------------------------

func:frame_push = NIL(Alias->:x) never fails { drop list_push(@x.frames, x.live.count); pass NIL; };
func:frame_pop = NIL(Alias->:x) never fails {
    if (x.frames.count == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    int64:mark = raw list_pop(@x.frames);
    drop list_truncate(@x.live, mark);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE VIEWS A `for` BINDING HOLDS (DEF-288, landing 155): a callee's store into
// the binding (`put(@h, string_bytes(t))`) records the view on the binding's own
// chain, which the escape analysis keeps by the binding's declaration in its
// parameter tables -- the binding is a block-scoped local, live for one iteration
// -- and those views are parties live over the loop's body, as a local holder's
// are live from its declaration. Until this landing only a PARAMETER's chain was
// read (`alias_fn`), so a view of a body local held by the binding froze nothing
// and the iteration's write to the local freed what the binding viewed (113 at
// both legs, the bytes reused). Pushed straight into the live set inside the
// loop's own frame, never into the pre-scan's: `alias_fn` makes every pre-scanned
// party whose holder is a declaration live at the function's entry.
func:push_loop_binding_parties = NIL(Alias->:x, DeclId:bind) never fails {
    int32:bsym = raw decl_symbol_of(x, bind.index);
    if (bsym == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:e = raw escape_param_view_ref_first(x.esc, bind.index);
    while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
        ViewRef:vr = raw escape_view_ref(x.esc, e);
        e = raw escape_view_ref_next(x.esc, e);
        if (vr.root == 0i32) { continue; }
        if ((vr.kind != (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) && (vr.kind != (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) { continue; }
        ExprId:place = ExprId{ index: vr.place };
        drop list_push(@x.live, Party{ site: place, kind: raw PARTY_VIEW(), root: vr.root, holder: bsym,
                                       place: place, view_kind: vr.kind, root_ptr: raw root_ident_is_pointer(x, place),
                                       path: vr.path });
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The parties admitted into this holder, made live now (its declaration).
func:register_holder = NIL(Alias->:x, int32:hsym) never fails {
    if (hsym == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.pre.count) {
        Party:pp = x.pre[i];
        if (pp.holder == hsym) { drop list_push(@x.live, pp); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:alias_stmt = NIL(Alias->:x, StmtId:id, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, id);
    if (depth <= 0i32) {
        drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this statement nests deeper than the aliasing analysis will follow, so its accesses cannot be checked",
            s.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    int32:dd = depth - 1i32;

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        drop frame_push(x);
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop alias_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) }, dd);
        }
        drop frame_pop(x);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        ExprId:init = raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, s);
        int32:hsym = raw decl_symbol(x, id, raw stmt_name(s));
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(init))) {
            int32:pk = raw party_kind_of(x, init);
            if (pk >= 0i32) {
                drop admit_value(x, init, pk, hsym);
            } else {
                drop refuse_holder_copy(x, init, hsym);
                drop acc_expr(x, init, raw ACC_READ(), dd);
            }
        }
        drop register_holder(x, hsym);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        ExprId:tgt = raw stmt_target(s);
        ExprId:val = raw stmt_assigned(s);
        drop acc_place(x, tgt, raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), dd);
        int32:pk2 = raw party_kind_of(x, val);
        if (pk2 >= 0i32) {
            int32:tsym = raw bare_local_symbol(x, tgt);
            if (tsym == 0i32) {
                // A `List`-element address (DEF-304) assigns like a plain one.
                if ((pk2 != (raw PARTY_PLAIN())) && (pk2 != (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()))) {
                    drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CLAIM_POSITION(),
                        "a `$$i`/`$$m` claim is a whole call argument or a pointer local's whole value (D-286), and this assigns one to a place that is not a local binding -- spell `@` for an address that claims nothing",
                        (raw ast_expr(x.ast, val)).span);
                    pass NIL;
                }
                drop acc_place(x, raw expr_operand(raw ast_expr(x.ast, val)), raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), dd);
                pass NIL;
            }
            // The party was registered at the holder's declaration (or the
            // function's entry): the claim is checked here as an access, once.
            drop admit_value(x, val, pk2, 0i32);
            pass NIL;
        }
        drop refuse_holder_copy(x, val, raw bare_local_symbol(x, tgt));
        drop acc_expr(x, val, raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_then(s), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_else(s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_body(x.ast, s), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_then(x.ast, s), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_end(x.ast, s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_for_iter(x.ast, s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        drop frame_push(x);
        drop push_loop_binding_parties(x, raw stmt_for_binding(s));
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_for_body(x.ast, s), dd);
        drop frame_pop(x);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...(raw stmt_counted_argc(x.ast, s))) {
            drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_counted_arg(x.ast, s, ai), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        }
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw stmt_counted_body(s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw pick_selector(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        for (int32:pa in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            drop alias_stmt(x, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), pa), dd);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickArm) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw arm_guard(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        drop alias_stmt(x, raw arm_body(s), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // A `defer` BODY RUNS AT ITS BLOCK'S EXIT: every party whose holder is
    // declared in an enclosing block is live for it, at any position.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        int64:mark = x.live.count;
        drop push_enclosing_parties(x, id);
        drop alias_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: s.a }, dd);
        drop list_truncate(@x.live, mark);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt)) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_operand(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt)    { pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) { pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFallStmt)     { pass NIL; }
    if (raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind)) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw stmt_expr(s), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_INTERNAL(),
        "this statement kind has no entry in the aliasing walk, so its accesses cannot be checked",
        s.span);
    pass NIL;
};

// The parties of the enclosing blocks not yet live -- a `defer` body's view.
// A holder's scope encloses the defer's statement when the holder's declaring
// scope is the defer's own scope or an ancestor of it; the defer's scope is
// read off the nearest enclosing declaration the pre-scan knows, which is
// conservative in the closed direction: a party whose holder is declared in
// a SIBLING block would be pushed too, and a sibling's party can only refuse.
func:push_enclosing_parties = NIL(Alias->:x, StmtId:defer_id) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.pre.count) {
        Party:pp = x.pre[i];
        bool:already = false;
        for (int64:j in 0i64...x.live.count) {
            if (x.live[j].site.index == pp.site.index) { already = true; }
        }
        if (already) { continue; }
        drop list_push(@x.live, pp);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A CLAIM OR PLAIN ADDRESS ADMITTED AS A WHOLE VALUE: the operand's index
// expressions are reads, the place is an access of the claim's own kind against
// every live party, and a claim without a named root is refused. `holder` is
// the declaring holder (registered by the caller) or 0.
func:admit_value = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:site, int32:kind, int32:holder) never fails {
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, site);
    ExprId:place = raw expr_operand(n);
    int32:akind = raw ACC_WRITE();
    if (kind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) { akind = raw ACC_SHARED(); }
    if (kind == (raw PARTY_EXCLUSIVE())) { akind = raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE(); }
    if ((kind != (raw PARTY_PLAIN())) && (kind != (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()))) {
        if ((raw place_root_symbol(x, place)) == 0i32) {
            drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CLAIM_POSITION(),
                "a `$$i`/`$$m` claim needs a place with a named root (D-286): a call's result or a dereference at the bottom names no binding whose accesses could be checked -- bind the value first, or spell `@`",
                n.span);
            pass NIL;
        }
    }
    drop acc_indices(x, place, raw ALIAS_DEPTH());
    drop check_access(x, place, akind, site, n.span);
    pass NIL;
};

// A PLAIN ADDRESS ADMITTED AS AN ARGUMENT OF A KNOWN CALLEE (D-325): the claims
// see the whole place as D-286 says; the view parties see the paths the callee
// writes below it, each an access of its own.
func:admit_written = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:site, int32:callee, int32:pos) never fails {
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, site);
    ExprId:place = raw expr_operand(n);
    drop acc_indices(x, place, raw ALIAS_DEPTH());
    drop check_access_ex(x, place, 0i32, raw ACC_WRITE(), site, n.span, raw CHECK_CLAIMS());
    drop check_written(x, place, callee, pos, n.span);
    pass NIL;
};

// The view parties against what a callee writes through a place handed to it
// at position `pos`: nothing when it writes nothing; the whole place when the
// escape analysis could not read it; each written path otherwise.
func:check_written = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:callee, int32:pos, Span:at) never fails {
    drop check_written_mode(x, place, callee, pos, at, raw CHECK_VIEWS());
    pass NIL;
};

func:check_written_mode = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:callee, int32:pos, Span:at,
                              int32:mode) never fails {
    int32:e = raw escape_mut_first(x.esc, callee, pos);
    if (e == (0i32 - 2i32)) {
        drop check_access_ex(x, place, 0i32, raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), at, mode);
        pass NIL;
    }
    while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
        if (raw check_access_reported(x, place, raw escape_mut_path(x.esc, e), raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), at, mode)) { pass NIL; }
        e = raw escape_mut_next(x.esc, e);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE VIEW PARTIES AGAINST WHAT A CALLEE WRITES THROUGH A SLICE ARGUMENT
// (DEF-289's second face, landing 157): each written path below the callee's
// slice parameter, composed with the argument -- for a RANGE of an array or a
// `List` the path's slice-level steps give way to the range's own step
// (`escape_slice_rest_path`: the element the callee names is one of the
// range's, at the range step's position) -- or the whole argument for a callee
// the escape analysis cannot read. The argument's own view party (a range view
// as a whole argument is one, for the call) is the access's own and is skipped.
// A RANGE OF A SLICE OR OF A RANGE (DEF-297, landing 159) is composed as a range
// of storage is, at its trailing run's FIRST range (`escape_first_trailing_range`):
// composed at the argument itself, the callee's element step stood one position
// past the range's, and a later field could read disjoint (`sl[0i64...1i64]`
// handed a callee writing `sl[0i64].o` under a view of `sl[0i64].o.x`: 113 at
// both legs on landing 158's compiler). A slice binding or field handed to a
// callee the analysis cannot read is written through WHOLE: its targets too.
func:check_written_slice = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:a, int32:callee, int32:pos, Span:at) never fails {
    ExprId:pl = raw escape_first_trailing_range(x.esc, a);
    bool:on_rng = !(raw expr_is_none(pl));
    if (!on_rng) { pl = a; }
    int32:e = raw escape_mut_first(x.esc, callee, pos);
    if (e == (0i32 - 2i32)) {
        if (raw check_access_reported(x, pl, 0i32, raw ACC_WRITE(), a, at, raw CHECK_VIEWS())) { pass NIL; }
        if (!on_rng) { discard(raw check_slice_targets(x, a, raw ACC_WRITE(), at, raw CHECK_VIEWS())); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
        int32:wp = raw escape_mut_path(x.esc, e);
        if (on_rng) { wp = raw escape_slice_rest_path(x.esc, wp); }
        if (raw check_access_reported(x, pl, wp, raw ACC_WRITE(), a, at, raw CHECK_VIEWS())) { pass NIL; }
        e = raw escape_mut_next(x.esc, e);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A HOLDER IS USED, NOT COPIED (D-286): a value that is a bare identifier
// holding a live claim, or a literal carrying one, cannot initialise or be
// assigned to another binding.
func:refuse_holder_copy = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:val, int32:target_sym) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(val)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, val);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if (raw sym_holds_claim(x, n.a)) {
            drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CLAIM_POSITION(),
                "a binding that holds a `$$i`/`$$m` claim is used, not copied (D-286): the claim's life would follow the copy where this walk cannot see it -- pass it down, or spell the claim `@`",
                n.span);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:sym_holds_claim = bool(Alias->:x, int32:sym) never fails {
    if (sym == 0i32) { pass false; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.live.count) {
        Party:p = x.live[i];
        if (p.holder != sym) { continue; }
        // A CLAIM, not a view: a view is a VALUE and is copied and passed
        // freely (D-325 freezes its root, never its holder's uses).
        if ((p.kind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) || (p.kind == (raw PARTY_EXCLUSIVE()))) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A WRITE-CAPABLE ACCESS THROUGH A SHARED CLAIM'S HOLDER (D-286: shared means
// readers), asked of the holder's symbol wherever a write reaches its storage:
// a place ROOTED at it (`p.f = v`, the rule's first home) and, since DEF-123
// (1.6.1d step 1; the library listener's F-008), a DEREFERENCE of it -- `(<-p) =
// v`, `move(<-p)`, `@(<-p)`, a pointer-receiver call on `<-p` -- which bottoms
// in no named root and was walked as a read of `p`. True when reported.
func:refuse_shared_holder_write = bool(Alias->:x, int32:holder, Span:at) never fails {
    if (holder == 0i32) { pass false; }
    for (int64:h in 0i64...x.live.count) {
        Party:hp = x.live[h];
        if ((hp.kind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) && (hp.holder == holder)) {
            string:m = string_concat("a write-capable access through `", raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, holder)).name));
            m = string_concat(m, "`, which holds ");
            m = string_concat(m, raw party_spelling(x, hp));
            m = string_concat(m, " (a SHARED claim: readers only, D-286) -- claim it `$$m` to write through it");
            drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CONFLICT(), move(m), at);
            pass true;
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// THE HOLDER A PLACE BOTTOMS IN: the bare pointer binding under a chain of
// `.`/`[]` steps whose bottom is `<-p` (`(<-p)`, `(<-p).f`, `(<-p)[i]`), or 0.
func:deref_holder_of = int32(Alias->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) { cur = raw expr_lhs(n); continue; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { pass (raw bare_local_symbol(x, raw expr_operand(n))); }
        pass 0i32;
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

func:sym_holds_shared_claim = bool(Alias->:x, int32:sym) never fails {
    if (sym == 0i32) { pass false; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...x.live.count) {
        Party:p = x.live[i];
        if (p.holder != sym) { continue; }
        if (p.kind == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A SHARED CLAIM, OR A POINTER HOLDING ONE, HANDED TO A CALLEE THAT WRITES
// THROUGH THAT POSITION (DEF-123 (b)): the callee's mutation summary (D-325)
// decides -- a known callee that writes nothing through it admits the reader
// it is; a written path refuses; a callee the analysis cannot see (a `dyn`
// method, a function value) refuses, the closed direction every walk here
// takes; a bare or `#` builtin has no summary and the reference's row is its
// reading, so it admits. `holder` names the pointer binding when the claim
// travels through one (`f(p)`, `p.m()`), 0 for the claim spelled as the argument.
func:refuse_shared_to_writer = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:call, int32:pos, int32:holder, Span:at) never fails {
    if (raw escape_call_is_bare_builtin(x.esc, call)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:cn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, call);
    if (cn.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) { pass NIL; }
    int32:cf = raw escape_call_fn(x.esc, call);
    int32:e = raw escape_mut_first(x.esc, cf, pos);
    if (e == (0i32 - 1i32)) { pass NIL; }
    string:m = "a `$$i` claim";
    if (holder != 0i32) {
        m = string_concat("`", raw intern_get(x.it, (raw symtab_get(x.tab, holder)).name));
        m = string_concat(m, "`, which holds a `$$i` claim,");
    }
    m = string_concat(m, " is handed to a callee that may write through it (a SHARED claim: readers only, D-286)");
    if (cf <= 0i32) { m = string_concat(m, " -- the callee cannot be read here (a `dyn` method or a function value), so the closed answer stands"); }
    m = string_concat(m, " -- claim it `$$m`, or hand the callee `@` for an address that claims nothing");
    drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CONFLICT(), move(m), at);
    pass NIL;
};

// --- expressions ---------------------------------------------------------------------

// The index expressions inside a place are READS of their own.
func:acc_indices = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:depth) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass NIL; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
            cur = raw expr_operand(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n), raw ACC_READ(), depth - 1i32);
            cur = raw expr_lhs(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }   // DEF-272: `<-` is a step
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass NIL; }
        // a non-place base (a call, an operator, a deref of one): walked as an ordinary expression
        drop acc_expr(x, cur, raw ACC_READ(), depth - 1i32);
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Is this expression a place chain -- a name, or `.`/`[]` steps down to one?
func:is_place_chain = bool(Alias->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass false; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) { cur = raw expr_lhs(n); continue; }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }   // DEF-272: `<-` is a step
        pass (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr);
    }
    pass false;
};

// A PLACE ACCESSED AS A WHOLE in the given kind: its indices read, the access
// checked once at the top.
func:acc_place = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:place, int32:akind, ExprId:self_site, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(place)) { pass NIL; }
    // NOT A CHAIN DOWN TO A NAME (a call's result, a dereference, an operator
    // at the bottom): no named root, so the CHILDREN are walked as reads --
    // never the node itself, which would be this walk calling itself.
    // A write to a PART is a write-capable access of what holds it, so the
    // access kind travels down to the bottom -- where a dereference of a shared
    // holder refuses it (DEF-123); a call or an operator there ignores it.
    if (!(raw is_place_chain(x, place))) {
        ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, place);
        if ((pn.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (pn.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
            drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_operand(pn), akind, depth);
            pass NIL;
        }
        if (pn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(pn), akind, depth);
            drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(pn), raw ACC_READ(), depth);
            pass NIL;
        }
        drop acc_expr(x, place, akind, depth);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `.len` OF AN ARRAY, A SLICE, A STRING OR A BUFFER READS NO ELEMENT.
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, place);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        if (raw is_len_read(x, n)) {
            drop acc_indices(x, raw expr_operand(n), depth);
            pass NIL;
        }
    }
    drop acc_indices(x, place, depth);
    drop check_access(x, place, akind, self_site, n.span);
    pass NIL;
};

func:is_len_read = bool(Alias->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    if (!(raw string_eq(raw intern_get(x.it, (raw expr_name(n)) =>! int32), "len"))) { pass false; }
    int32:bt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, raw expr_operand(n));
    if (bt == 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:bk = raw type_kind(x.types, bt);
    if (bk == (raw TY_POINTER())) { bk = raw type_kind(x.types, raw type_elem(x.types, bt)); }
    if (bk == (raw TY_ARRAY()))  { pass true; }
    if (bk == (raw TY_SLICE()))  { pass true; }
    if (bk == (raw TY_STRING())) { pass true; }
    if (bk == (raw TY_BUFFER())) { pass true; }
    pass false;
};

func:acc_window = NIL(Alias->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:depth) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        drop acc_expr(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, raw ACC_READ(), depth);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:acc_expr = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:id, int32:akind, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (depth <= 0i32) {
        drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this expression nests deeper than the aliasing analysis will follow, so its accesses cannot be checked",
            n.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    int32:dd = depth - 1i32;

    // A PLACE: one access, at the top of the chain. A dereference whose operand
    // is a chain -- `<-p`, `(<-p).f`, `(<-p)[i]` -- is a place rooted at the
    // pointer's name (DEF-272, landing 138), as `p.f` always was; a deref of
    // anything else keeps its own arm below.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr)
        || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)
        || ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) && (raw is_place_chain(x, id)))) {
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            ExprNode:ixn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, raw expr_rhs(n));
            // A RANGE VIEW hands out the base's address (D-249): write-capable
            // over the whole extent.
            if (ixn.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) {
                drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(ixn), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
                drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(ixn), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
                // ... against the CLAIMS; a second view of storage a view already
                // covers is a reader beside a reader for the view parties
                // (D-325): making it frees nothing.
                if (raw is_place_chain(x, id)) {
                    drop acc_indices(x, id, dd);
                    ExprNode:rvn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
                    drop check_access_ex(x, id, 0i32, raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), rvn.span, raw CHECK_CLAIMS());
                } else {
                    drop acc_place(x, id, raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), dd);
                }
                pass NIL;
            }
        }
        drop acc_place(x, id, akind, raw expr_none(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }

    // A CLAIM ANYWHERE ELSE THAN AN ADMITTING SITE (D-286): refused by name.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        drop acc_indices(x, raw expr_operand(n), dd);
        drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CLAIM_POSITION(),
            "a `$$i`/`$$m` claim is a whole call argument or a pointer local's whole value (D-286), and this one stands elsewhere -- in a literal, a `pass` value, a nested expression -- spell `@` for an address that claims nothing",
            n.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // A PLAIN ADDRESS IS A WRITE-CAPABLE ACCESS OF ITS PLACE.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        drop acc_place(x, raw expr_operand(n), raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `move(place)` vacates it: write-capable.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr) {
        drop acc_place(x, raw expr_operand(n), raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `<-(…)` OF SOMETHING THAT IS NOT A CHAIN (a call's result, an operator):
    // the pointee is no named root -- but a SHARED holder's pointee is
    // readers-only storage, and a write-capable access through it is D-286's
    // refusal (DEF-123). A deref of a chain is a place above (DEF-272).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) {
        if ((akind == (raw ACC_WRITE())) || (akind == (raw ACC_EXCLUSIVE()))) {
            discard(raw refuse_shared_holder_write(x, raw deref_holder_of(x, id), n.span));
        }
        drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        drop acc_call(x, id, n, raw expr_none(), (raw expr_list_start(n)) + (raw expr_generic_count(n)),
                      (raw expr_list_count(n)) - (raw expr_generic_count(n)), raw expr_callee(n), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // A SPAWN (DEF-148): `drop f(…)` on an `async` callee -- the escape
    // analysis's own reading of the spawn (`callee_is_async`) -- is remembered
    // while the call's arguments are walked, so `acc_call` can lend them.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) {
        ExprId:sp_op = raw expr_operand(n);
        ExprId:saved_spawn = x.spawn_call;
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(sp_op))) {
            ExprNode:sp_n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, sp_op);
            if (sp_n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
                if (raw callee_is_async(x.esc, sp_n)) { x.spawn_call = sp_op; }
            }
        }
        drop acc_expr(x, sp_op, raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        x.spawn_call = saved_spawn;
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        ExprId:recv = raw expr_operand(n);
        if ((raw exprtypes_ns_decl(x.etypes, id)) != 0i32) { recv = raw expr_none(); }
        drop acc_call(x, id, n, recv, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n), raw expr_none(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        drop acc_call(x, id, n, raw expr_none(), (raw expr_list_start(n)) + (raw builtin_generic_count(n)),
                      (raw expr_list_count(n)) - (raw builtin_generic_count(n)), raw expr_none(), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:cnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        int32:i = 1i32;
        while (i < cnt) decreases cnt - i {
            ExprId:v = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), i) };
            drop refuse_holder_copy(x, v, 0i32);
            drop acc_expr(x, v, raw ACC_READ(), dd);
            i = i + 2i32;
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprArrayLiteralExpr) {
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...(raw expr_list_count(n))) {
            ExprId:av = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), ai) };
            drop refuse_holder_copy(x, av, 0i32);
            drop acc_expr(x, av, raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        drop acc_expr(x, raw pickx_selector(n), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
        for (int32:pi in 0i32...(raw pickx_arm_count(n))) {
            drop alias_stmt(x, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pickx_arm_start(n), pi), dd);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    // EVERYTHING ELSE BY SHAPE: reads of the children.
    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LEAF())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_NONE())) {
        drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_INTERNAL(),
            "this expression kind has no entry in `expr_shape`, so the aliasing walk cannot reach its slots",
            n.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_CUSTOM())) {
        drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_INTERNAL(),
            "this expression kind has a custom shape the aliasing walk has no case for",
            n.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
        drop acc_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
        drop acc_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n), dd);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_TWO())) { pass NIL; }
    drop acc_expr(x, raw expr_third(n), raw ACC_READ(), dd);
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL: its claim arguments are live for the call, each checked against
// the outer parties and the call's own; the receiver is write-capable when the
// callee's first parameter is a pointer and the receiver expression is not one
// (the auto-ref the checker performs, 1.0.9b) and a read otherwise; a claim
// argument of a call whose RESULT can carry a pointer is refused (D-117 rule
// A: the result may point at it, and no holder's value could be compared).
func:acc_call = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, ExprId:recv, int32:start, int32:count,
                    ExprId:callee, int32:depth) never fails {
    drop acc_expr(x, callee, raw ACC_READ(), depth);
    int64:mark = x.live.count;
    int32:pos_base = 0i32;   // the receiver is position 0 of the callee's summary
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(recv))) { pos_base = 1i32; }
    bool:result_carries = false;
    int32:rty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id);
    if (rty != 0i32) { result_carries = raw carries_pointer_type(x.types, rty); }
    // The claim arguments become parties first.
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        int32:pk = raw party_kind_of(x, a);
        if (pk < 0i32) {
            // A VIEW EXPRESSION AS A WHOLE ARGUMENT (D-325): a view party of its
            // viewed place for the call -- `f(string_from_bytes(d.ptr, n), @d)`
            // hands a callee a view and a way to free what it views.
            drop push_call_view_party(x, a);
            continue;
        }
        if ((pk == (raw PARTY_PLAIN())) || (pk == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()))) { continue; }   // an address is no claim party (DEF-304: handled in the ordinary-arg loop)
        ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
        if (result_carries) {
            drop alias_err(x, raw BORROW_CLAIM_POSITION(),
                "a `$$i`/`$$m` claim cannot be an argument of a call whose result can carry a pointer (D-286, D-117 rule A): the callee decides what the result points at, and no holder's value could be compared -- spell `@`",
                an.span);
            continue;
        }
        int32:root = raw place_root_symbol(x, raw expr_operand(an));
        if (root == 0i32) { continue; }   // refused below as a claim without a root
        // A SHARED CLAIM TO A CALLEE THAT WRITES THROUGH IT (DEF-123 (b)).
        if (pk == (raw PARTY_SHARED())) { drop refuse_shared_to_writer(x, id, pos_base + i, 0i32, an.span); }
        drop list_push(@x.live, Party{ site: a, kind: pk, root: root, holder: 0i32,
                                       place: raw expr_operand(an), view_kind: 0i32, root_ptr: false, path: 0i32 });
    }
    // The receiver.
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(recv))) {
        int32:rk = raw ACC_READ();
        int32:ft = raw exprtypes_callee_ft(x.etypes, id);
        bool:ptr_recv = true;   // unknown callee: conservative
        if (ft != 0i32) {
            ptr_recv = false;
            if ((raw type_param_count_of(x.types, ft)) > 0i32) {
                int32:p0 = raw type_param_at_of(x.ast, x.types, ft, 0i32);
                if ((raw type_kind(x.types, p0)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { ptr_recv = true; }
            }
        }
        int32:rxt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, recv);
        bool:recv_is_ptr = false;
        if (rxt != 0i32) {
            if ((raw type_kind(x.types, rxt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { recv_is_ptr = true; }
        }
        // THE POINTER VALUE PASSED AS THE RECEIVER (DEF-123 (b)): `p.m()` with
        // `p` a pointer holding a SHARED claim and `m` taking `Self->` writes
        // through the claim as `f(p)` does.
        if (ptr_recv && recv_is_ptr) {
            int32:rsym = raw bare_local_symbol(x, recv);
            if (rsym != 0i32) { if (raw sym_holds_shared_claim(x, rsym)) {
                drop refuse_shared_to_writer(x, id, 0i32, rsym, (raw ast_expr(x.ast, recv)).span);
            } }
        }
        bool:recv_ptr_param = ptr_recv;   // the method takes a pointer receiver (Self->)
        if (recv_is_ptr) { ptr_recv = false; }
        if (ptr_recv) { rk = raw ACC_WRITE(); }
        int32:rcallee = raw escape_call_fn(x.esc, id);
        // THE RECEIVER OF AN OPERATION IN A CROSSING KIND'S CONCURRENT SET
        // (DEF-148): a builtin method of one of D-180's five kinds that the
        // type's contract permits while a task holds it -- `s.alloc(v)`,
        // `m.acquire(d)` -- is checked against every party but the LENT ones.
        // `destroy`, an operation outside the set, keeps every party.
        bool:lent_ok = false;
        if ((ft == 0i32) && (rcallee == 0i32) && (rxt != 0i32) && (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr)) {
            int32:rxk = raw type_kind(x.types, rxt);
            if (rxk == (raw TY_POINTER())) { rxk = raw type_kind(x.types, raw type_elem(x.types, rxt)); }
            if (raw spawn_crossing_kind(rxk)) {
                lent_ok = raw crossing_concurrent_method(rxk, raw intern_get(x.it, n.payload =>! int32));
            }
        }
        if (ptr_recv && (rcallee > 0i32) && (raw is_place_chain(x, recv))) {
            // the implicit `@recv`: what the method writes through it
            drop acc_indices(x, recv, depth);
            ExprNode:rvn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, recv);
            drop check_access_ex(x, recv, 0i32, raw ACC_WRITE(), raw expr_none(), rvn.span, raw CHECK_CLAIMS());
            drop check_written(x, recv, rcallee, 0i32, rvn.span);
        } else {
            if (lent_ok && (raw is_place_chain(x, recv))) {
                x.skip_lent = true;
                drop acc_place(x, recv, rk, raw expr_none(), depth);
                x.skip_lent = false;
            } else {
                drop acc_expr(x, recv, rk, depth);
            }
            // A POINTER-VALUE RECEIVER OF A `Self->` METHOD (DEF-302, landing 160):
            // `hp.set()` where `set` writes `self.o` writes through what `hp`
            // points at, as `f(hp)` does (DEF-275); checked against the views
            // there (`check_written` → `check_pointer_targets`). The else branch
            // read `recv` only; a by-value receiver (`recv_ptr_param` false) gets
            // a copy and writes through nothing. A call-result pointer receiver
            // (`(raw idp(@h)).set()`, DEF-305) is no place chain and resolves by
            // rule A in `check_pointer_targets`' call-result arm.
            if (recv_ptr_param && recv_is_ptr && (rcallee > 0i32)) {
                drop check_written(x, recv, rcallee, 0i32, (raw ast_expr(x.ast, recv)).span);
            }
        }
    }
    // Every ordinary argument as an access against the outer parties and all
    // of the call's claims. A PLAIN ADDRESS handed to a KNOWN callee is, for the
    // view parties, an access of exactly what that callee WRITES through it
    // (its mutation summary, D-325): `@r` handed to `fold_gave_up` writes
    // nothing and conflicts with no view of `r`; handed to `fold_const` it
    // writes `r.fold_counting` and conflicts only with a view of that. The
    // claims keep D-286's whole-argument rule.
    int32:callee_fn = raw escape_call_fn(x.esc, id);
    for (int32:j in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:a2 = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, j) };
        int32:pk2 = raw party_kind_of(x, a2);
        if (pk2 >= 0i32) {
            if ((pk2 == (raw PARTY_PLAIN())) || (pk2 == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()))) {   // a `List`-element address as an argument is handled as a plain one (DEF-304: the callee road, the freeze fires on the reallocating op itself)
                if (callee_fn > 0i32) { drop admit_written(x, a2, callee_fn, pos_base + j); }
                else { drop admit_value(x, a2, pk2, 0i32); }
            }
            continue;
        }
        // A POINTER HOLDING A SHARED CLAIM, HANDED BY VALUE (DEF-123 (b)): the
        // callee writes through the value as it would through the claim itself.
        int32:hsym2 = raw bare_local_symbol(x, a2);
        if (hsym2 != 0i32) {
            int32:ht2 = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a2);
            if (ht2 != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(x.types, ht2)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
                if (raw sym_holds_shared_claim(x, hsym2)) {
                    drop refuse_shared_to_writer(x, id, pos_base + j, hsym2, (raw ast_expr(x.ast, a2)).span);
                }
            } }
        }
        drop refuse_holder_copy_arg(x, a2, result_carries);
        // A POINTER VALUE HANDED TO A CALLEE (DEF-275): the callee writes through
        // the value as it would through `@place` -- what its mutation summary
        // says it writes (the whole pointee for a callee the escape analysis
        // cannot read; nothing for a bare or `#` builtin, whose aliasing is the
        // reference's row) is an access of what the pointer reaches, against
        // the view parties rooted at the pointer's name.
        int32:at2 = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a2);
        if ((at2 != 0i32) && (!(raw escape_call_is_bare_builtin(x.esc, id))) && (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr)) {
            if (((raw type_kind(x.types, at2)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) && (raw is_place_chain(x, a2))) {
                drop check_written(x, a2, callee_fn, pos_base + j, (raw ast_expr(x.ast, a2)).span);
            }
            // A SLICE HANDED TO A CALLEE (DEF-289's second face, landing 157):
            // the callee writes the elements the slice views -- what its
            // mutation summary says it writes below its slice parameter -- and
            // that is an access of the argument's storage against the view
            // parties rooted where the argument roots (a range `arr[lo...hi]`
            // at `arr`, a slice binding at the binding).
            if (((raw type_kind(x.types, at2)) == (raw TY_SLICE())) && (raw is_place_chain(x, a2))) {
                if (!(raw type_slice_fixed(x.types, at2))) {   // read-only through it (D-348)
                    drop check_written_slice(x, a2, callee_fn, pos_base + j, (raw ast_expr(x.ast, a2)).span);
                }
            }
            // A SLICE NO PLACE NAMES handed to a callee that writes through it
            // (DEF-301, landing 159): a call's result, a ternary -- each storage
            // its value views, whole, against the view parties there.
            if (((raw type_kind(x.types, at2)) == (raw TY_SLICE())) && (!(raw is_place_chain(x, a2)))) {
                if (!(raw type_slice_fixed(x.types, at2))) {
                    if ((raw escape_mut_first(x.esc, callee_fn, pos_base + j)) != (0i32 - 1i32)) {
                        discard(raw check_slice_targets(x, a2, raw ACC_WRITE(), (raw ast_expr(x.ast, a2)).span, raw CHECK_VIEWS()));
                    }
                }
            }
            // A POINTER NO PLACE NAMES handed to a callee that writes through it
            // (DEF-305): a call's result (`wp(raw idp(@h))`) -- resolved by rule A
            // (`escape_pointer_targets`), the callee's written path against the
            // view parties at the storage it points at (check_written →
            // check_pointer_targets' call-result arm). The place-chain twin is
            // the branch above.
            if (((raw type_kind(x.types, at2)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) && (!(raw is_place_chain(x, a2)))) {
                drop check_written(x, a2, callee_fn, pos_base + j, (raw ast_expr(x.ast, a2)).span);
            }
        }
        drop acc_expr(x, a2, raw ACC_READ(), depth);
    }
    // Then each claim against the outer parties and the EARLIER claims of the
    // call -- one report per conflicting pair, at the later claim.
    drop list_truncate(@x.live, mark);
    for (int32:k in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:a3 = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, k) };
        int32:pk3 = raw party_kind_of(x, a3);
        if (pk3 < 0i32) { continue; }
        if ((pk3 == (raw PARTY_PLAIN())) || (pk3 == (raw PARTY_ELEM_ADDR()))) { continue; }   // an address is no claim (DEF-304)
        if (result_carries) { continue; }
        drop admit_value(x, a3, pk3, 0i32);
        ExprNode:an3 = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a3);
        int32:root3 = raw place_root_symbol(x, raw expr_operand(an3));
        if (root3 == 0i32) { continue; }
        drop list_push(@x.live, Party{ site: a3, kind: pk3, root: root3, holder: 0i32,
                                       place: raw expr_operand(an3), view_kind: 0i32, root_ptr: false, path: 0i32 });
    }
    drop list_truncate(@x.live, mark);
    // A SPAWN LENDS ITS CROSSINGS UNTIL THE BLOCK'S JOIN (DEF-148, 1.6.1e
    // step 1): each argument that is a pointer to one of D-180's five kinds --
    // `@s` of a binding, or a pointer binding handed on -- becomes a LENT
    // party on its root, sited at the call, live until the enclosing block's
    // `frame_pop`. The party is pushed after the call's own parties are gone,
    // and the callee's mutation summary is then read against it for the
    // spawn's own `@s`: a task that writes or moves out what it was lent is
    // refused at the spawn, as a later `destroy` by the owner is.
    if (id.index == x.spawn_call.index) {
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(x.spawn_call))) { drop lend_spawn_args(x, id, start, count, pos_base, callee_fn); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:lend_spawn_args = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:id, int32:start, int32:count, int32:pos_base,
                           int32:callee_fn) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        int32:aty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
        if (aty == 0i32) { continue; }
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, aty)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { continue; }
        if (!(raw spawn_crossing_kind(raw type_kind(x.types, raw type_elem(x.types, aty))))) { continue; }
        ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
        ExprId:place = raw expr_none();
        bool:root_ptr = false;
        if (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
            place = raw expr_operand(an);
        } else {
            if (an.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { continue; }
            place = a;
            root_ptr = true;
        }
        int32:root = raw place_root_symbol(x, place);
        if (root == 0i32) { continue; }
        drop list_push(@x.live, Party{ site: id, kind: raw PARTY_LENT(), root: root, holder: 0i32,
                                       place: place, view_kind: 0i32, root_ptr: root_ptr, path: 0i32 });
        if ((an.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) && (callee_fn > 0i32)) {
            drop check_written_mode(x, place, callee_fn, pos_base + i, an.span, raw CHECK_LENT());
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A view expression standing as a whole call argument -- a view-maker's call
// (`string_bytes(s)`, `string_from_bytes(p, n)`), a `#` view builtin, or a
// range view (`l[lo...hi]`) -- is a VIEW party of its viewed place for the
// call (D-325). Anything else is an ordinary argument; a view NESTED inside
// one (`f(g(string_bytes(s)))`) is a temporary the escape walk already reads.
func:push_call_view_party = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:a) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    ExprId:vp = raw escape_view_place(x.esc, n);
    if (raw expr_is_none(vp)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprId:place = vp;
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) { place = a; }   // the range step is part of the path
    int32:root = raw place_root_symbol(x, place);
    if (root == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop list_push(@x.live, Party{ site: a, kind: raw PARTY_VIEW(), root: root, holder: 0i32,
                                   place: place, view_kind: raw VIEW_DIRECT(),
                                   root_ptr: raw root_ident_is_pointer(x, place), path: 0i32 });
    pass NIL;
};

// A holder passed to a call whose result can carry a pointer is a copy the walk
// cannot follow (rule A); passed to any other call it is a use.
func:refuse_holder_copy_arg = NIL(Alias->:x, ExprId:a, bool:result_carries) never fails {
    if (!result_carries) { pass NIL; }
    drop refuse_holder_copy(x, a, 0i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// `carries_pointer` is the escape analysis's, over a type table alone.
func:carries_pointer_type = bool(TypeTable->:types, int32:ty) never fails {
    pass (raw carries_pointer_ty(types, ty, raw CARRY_FUEL()));
};
